window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b231-4ad6208d44537a00.json"]={sha256:"4ad6208d44537a005447084621e4e5b628a3182831c4aab1cfd3f28eefffa3ff",value:{"id":"b231","title":"混凝土重力壩分塊澆築","titleEn":"Block-by-block concrete gravity-dam construction","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課以混凝土重力壩分塊澆築為入口，深入澆塊熱歷程、層面品質與重力壩荷載路徑。十個單元各自對應不同的荷載路徑、能量交換或監測問題，從守恆式建立量化估算，再檢查量測配置是否能辨認真正失效原因。工程史實只採用列明範圍的公開一手資料；所有模型輸入另標為教學假設，成果是可追溯的工程判讀紀錄。","summaryEn":"Using Block-by-block concrete gravity-dam construction as its entry point, this course examines block thermal histories, lift-joint quality and gravity-dam load paths. Ten units address different load paths, energy exchanges or monitoring questions, starting with conservation-based estimates and testing whether observations distinguish failure causes. Historical statements use scoped primary evidence. Numerical model inputs are separately identified as teaching assumptions, producing a traceable engineering interpretation record.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-systems","subcategoryTitle":"防潮、航運與大壩施工","subcategoryTitleEn":"Tidal barriers, navigation and dam construction","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-systems","learningTags":["water","water-systems","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-dam","architectureNodes":[["絕熱溫升與膠結材","Adiabatic rise and binder heat"],["層面剪力與有效正應力","Lift-joint shear and effective stress"],["冷卻水能量移除","Cooling-water heat removal"],["接縫開度與止水變形","Joint opening and waterstop deformation"],["澆塊幾何與材料追溯","Block geometry and material traceability"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-dam","labels":["絕熱溫升與膠結材","層面剪力與有效正應力","冷卻水能量移除","接縫開度與止水變形","澆塊幾何與材料追溯"],"labelsEn":["Adiabatic rise and binder heat","Lift-joint shear and effective stress","Cooling-water heat removal","Joint opening and waterstop deformation","Block geometry and material traceability"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"本課原創比較練習分兩個相互獨立的物理模型。教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設膠結材180 kg/m³、累積放熱250 kJ/kg、混凝土體積熱容量2.4 MJ/(m³·K)，絕熱溫升18.75 K；不是實際峰值溫度。教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設澆塊600 m³、有效供應率75 m³/h，純澆置需8 h；若停機1.5 h則9.5 h，未計振實和局部覆蓋順序。先逐一圈出公式內的控制體、力方向或時間尺度，再把每項輸入的量綱換成一致單位。第二人只根據輸入重算結果，不抄第一人的中間數字。最後指出這兩個估算尚未包含的空間變化、非線性及量測誤差；若將結果用於另一座工程，必須重建其幾何、材料與邊界條件，不能挪用本練習的假設。","textEn":"This original comparison exercise uses two independent physical models. Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume binder 180 kg/m³, cumulative heat 250 kJ/kg and volumetric heat capacity 2.4 MJ/(m³·K). Adiabatic rise is 18.75 K, not the actual peak temperature. Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume block volume 600 m³ and effective supply 75 m³/h. Placement requires eight hours, or 9.5 h with a 1.5 h outage, excluding local compaction and coverage sequence. First identify the control volume, force direction or time scale in each relation, then convert every input to consistent units. A second reviewer recalculates from the inputs without copying intermediate numbers. Finally identify spatial variability, nonlinear effects and measurement errors omitted by both estimates. Transfer to another structure requires rebuilding its geometry, material description and boundary conditions; the assumed classroom inputs are not transferable design or operating parameters.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b231-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「絕熱溫升與膠結材」與「澆置供應與冷縫風險」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Adiabatic rise and binder heat\" and \"Placement supply and cold joints\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b231-v15-01","title":"絕熱溫升與膠結材：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Adiabatic rise and binder heat: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「絕熱溫升與膠結材」如何影響混凝土重力壩分塊澆築的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Adiabatic rise and binder heat” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Block-by-block concrete gravity-dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"大體積混凝土內部散熱慢，膠結材水化熱會累積。絕熱溫升把放熱量和材料熱容量連結，但真實澆塊還有表面交換、骨材溫度與時間效應。 假設膠結材180 kg/m³、累積放熱250 kJ/kg、混凝土體積熱容量2.4 MJ/(m³·K)，絕熱溫升18.75 K；不是實際峰值溫度。 把最終總放熱瞬間施加會錯估早期峰值，忽略表面散熱則會過度保守或失去梯度資訊。相同膠結材用量也不保證不同配方具有相同放熱速率。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「絕熱溫升與膠結材」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Heat accumulates inside mass concrete because dissipation is slow. Adiabatic rise links binder heat to material heat capacity, while actual blocks also exchange heat at surfaces and depend on aggregate temperature and time. Assume binder 180 kg/m³, cumulative heat 250 kJ/kg and volumetric heat capacity 2.4 MJ/(m³·K). Adiabatic rise is 18.75 K, not the actual peak temperature. Applying ultimate heat instantly misstates early peaks, while neglecting surface loss removes gradient information. Equal binder content also does not guarantee equal heat-release rates across different cementitious formulations. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Adiabatic rise and binder heat” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設膠結材180 kg/m³、累積放熱250 kJ/kg、混凝土體積熱容量2.4 MJ/(m³·K)，絕熱溫升18.75 K；不是實際峰值溫度。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume binder 180 kg/m³, cumulative heat 250 kJ/kg and volumetric heat capacity 2.4 MJ/(m³·K).","failure":"常見誤解：「絕熱溫升就是工地澆塊必定量到的最高溫度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adiabatic temperature rise is the highest temperature that every placed block must reach.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「絕熱溫升與膠結材」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Adiabatic rise and binder heat”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-01-k1","title":"絕熱溫升與膠結材","titleEn":"Adiabatic rise and binder heat","text":"大體積混凝土內部散熱慢，膠結材水化熱會累積。絕熱溫升把放熱量和材料熱容量連結，但真實澆塊還有表面交換、骨材溫度與時間效應。","textEn":"Heat accumulates inside mass concrete because dissipation is slow. Adiabatic rise links binder heat to material heat capacity, while actual blocks also exchange heat at surfaces and depend on aggregate temperature and time.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：絕熱溫升就是工地澆塊必定量到的最高溫度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adiabatic temperature rise is the highest temperature that every placed block must reach. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「絕熱溫升與膠結材」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Adiabatic rise and binder heat\" is correct?","options":["絕熱溫升就是工地澆塊必定量到的最高溫度。","大體積混凝土內部散熱慢，膠結材水化熱會累積。","只要最後總澆置方量正確，局部冷縫就不會影響壩體。"],"optionsEn":["Adiabatic temperature rise is the highest temperature that every placed block must reach.","Heat accumulates inside mass concrete because dissipation is slow.","Correct final placed volume means local cold joints cannot affect the dam."],"answer":1,"explanation":"大體積混凝土內部散熱慢，膠結材水化熱會累積。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Heat accumulates inside mass concrete because dissipation is slow. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b231-v15-02","title":"絕熱溫升與膠結材：定量估算","titleEn":"Adiabatic rise and binder heat: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「絕熱溫升與膠結材」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Adiabatic rise and binder heat” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設膠結材180 kg/m³、累積放熱250 kJ/kg、混凝土體積熱容量2.4 MJ/(m³·K)，絕熱溫升18.75 K；不是實際峰值溫度。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume binder 180 kg/m³, cumulative heat 250 kJ/kg and volumetric heat capacity 2.4 MJ/(m³·K). Adiabatic rise is 18.75 K, not the actual peak temperature. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以材料量熱試驗取得放熱歷線，核對膠結材來源與配比，再比較澆塊中心與表面溫度；用能量平衡檢查溫度初值，並分列模板、氣溫與冷卻邊界。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Obtain heat-release histories from calorimetry, checking binder source and mixture proportions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設膠結材180 kg/m³、累積放熱250 kJ/kg、混凝土體積熱容量2.4 MJ/(m³·K)，絕熱溫升18.75 K；不是實際峰值溫度。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume binder 180 kg/m³, cumulative heat 250 kJ/kg and volumetric heat capacity 2.4 MJ/(m³·K). Adiabatic rise is 18.75 K, not the actual peak temperature.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「絕熱溫升與膠結材」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Adiabatic rise and binder heat\", which statement holds?","options":["澆塊厚度加倍只會讓熱擴散時間加倍。","成熟度達到固定數字就代表所有混凝土具有同一強度。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設膠結材180 kg/m³、累積放熱250 kJ/kg、混凝土體積熱容量2.4 MJ/(m³·K)，絕熱溫升18.75 K。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling block thickness only doubles the thermal diffusion time.","A fixed maturity value means every concrete mixture has the same strength.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume binder 180 kg/m³, cumulative heat 250 kJ/kg and volumetric heat capacity 2.4 MJ/(m³·K)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設膠結材180 kg/m³、累積放熱250 kJ/kg、混凝土體積熱容量2.4 MJ/(m³·K)，絕熱溫升18.75 K；不是實際峰值溫度。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume binder 180 kg/m³, cumulative heat 250 kJ/kg and volumetric heat capacity 2.4 MJ/(m³·K). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b231-v15-03","title":"絕熱溫升與膠結材：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Adiabatic rise and binder heat: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「絕熱溫升與膠結材」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Adiabatic rise and binder heat” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以材料量熱試驗取得放熱歷線，核對膠結材來源與配比，再比較澆塊中心與表面溫度；用能量平衡檢查溫度初值，並分列模板、氣溫與冷卻邊界。以初始骨材溫度獨立檢查入倉混凝土熱量。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Obtain heat-release histories from calorimetry, checking binder source and mixture proportions. Compare block-core and surface temperatures, verify initial conditions by energy balance, and list formwork, air-temperature and cooling boundaries separately. Independently check placed-concrete initial heat against measured aggregate temperature. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以絕熱溫升與膠結材編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。以材料量熱試驗取得放熱歷線，核對膠結材來源與配比，再比較澆塊中心與表面溫度；用能量平衡檢查溫度初值，並分列模板、氣溫與冷卻邊界。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for adiabatic rise and binder heat, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Obtain heat-release histories from calorimetry, checking binder source and mixture proportions. Compare block-core and surface temperatures, verify initial conditions by energy balance, and list formwork, air-temperature and cooling boundaries separately.","failure":"注意干擾：把最終總放熱瞬間施加會錯估早期峰值，忽略表面散熱則會過度保守或失去梯度資訊。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Applying ultimate heat instantly misstates early peaks, while neglecting surface loss removes gradient information. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以材料量熱試驗取得放熱歷線，核對膠結材來源與配比，再比較澆塊中心與表面溫度；用能量平衡檢查溫度初值，並分列模板、氣溫與冷卻邊界。以初始骨材溫度獨立檢查入倉混凝土熱量。","textEn":"Obtain heat-release histories from calorimetry, checking binder source and mixture proportions. Compare block-core and surface temperatures, verify initial conditions by energy balance, and list formwork, air-temperature and cooling boundaries separately. Independently check placed-concrete initial heat against measured aggregate temperature.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以絕熱溫升與膠結材編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。以材料量熱試驗取得放熱歷線，核對膠結材來源與配比，再比較澆塊中心與表面溫度；用能量平衡檢查溫度初值，並分列模板、氣溫與冷卻邊界。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for adiabatic rise and binder heat, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Obtain heat-release histories from calorimetry, checking binder source and mixture proportions. Compare block-core and surface temperatures, verify initial conditions by energy balance, and list formwork, air-temperature and cooling boundaries separately.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「絕熱溫升與膠結材」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Adiabatic rise and binder heat\"?","options":["以材料量熱試驗取得放熱歷線，核對膠結材來源與配比，再比較澆塊中心與表面溫度；用能量平衡檢查溫度初值，並分列模板、氣溫與冷卻邊界。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","混凝土剛澆入就已完全自立，所以模板不承受液態側壓。"],"optionsEn":["Obtain heat-release histories from calorimetry, checking binder source and mixture proportions.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Freshly placed concrete is immediately self-supporting and exerts no fluid-like form pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以材料量熱試驗取得放熱歷線，核對膠結材來源與配比，再比較澆塊中心與表面溫度；用能量平衡檢查溫度初值，並分列模板、氣溫與冷卻邊界。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Obtain heat-release histories from calorimetry, checking binder source and mixture proportions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b231-v15-04","title":"絕熱溫升與膠結材：失效診斷","titleEn":"Adiabatic rise and binder heat: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「絕熱溫升與膠結材」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Adiabatic rise and binder heat” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把最終總放熱瞬間施加會錯估早期峰值，忽略表面散熱則會過度保守或失去梯度資訊。相同膠結材用量也不保證不同配方具有相同放熱速率。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Applying ultimate heat instantly misstates early peaks, while neglecting surface loss removes gradient information. Equal binder content also does not guarantee equal heat-release rates across different cementitious formulations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：相同膠結材用量也不保證不同配方具有相同放熱速率。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Equal binder content also does not guarantee equal heat-release rates across different cementitious formulations.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「絕熱溫升就是工地澆塊必定量到的最高溫度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adiabatic temperature rise is the highest temperature that every placed block must reach.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把最終總放熱瞬間施加會錯估早期峰值，忽略表面散熱則會過度保守或失去梯度資訊。相同膠結材用量也不保證不同配方具有相同放熱速率。","textEn":"Applying ultimate heat instantly misstates early peaks, while neglecting surface loss removes gradient information. Equal binder content also does not guarantee equal heat-release rates across different cementitious formulations.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「絕熱溫升與膠結材」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Adiabatic rise and binder heat\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把最終總放熱瞬間施加會錯估早期峰值，忽略表面散熱則會過度保守或失去梯度資訊。","只要最後總澆置方量正確，局部冷縫就不會影響壩體。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Applying ultimate heat instantly misstates early peaks, while neglecting surface loss removes gradient information.","Correct final placed volume means local cold joints cannot affect the dam."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把最終總放熱瞬間施加會錯估早期峰值，忽略表面散熱則會過度保守或失去梯度資訊。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Applying ultimate heat instantly misstates early peaks, while neglecting surface loss removes gradient information. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b231-v15-05","title":"澆置供應與冷縫風險：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Placement supply and cold joints: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「澆置供應與冷縫風險」如何影響混凝土重力壩分塊澆築的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Placement supply and cold joints” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Block-by-block concrete gravity-dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"分塊澆築要求連續供料與有序覆蓋，供應率不足會延長新舊料接觸時間。總日產量達標不代表每一局部層面都在可接受條件下接續。 假設澆塊600 m³、有效供應率75 m³/h，純澆置需8 h；若停機1.5 h則9.5 h，未計振實和局部覆蓋順序。 同一停機時間在不同溫度下會產生不同接縫狀態，盲目加水恢復工作性又會改變材料品質。若只補足少澆的方量，已形成的弱層不會自動消失。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「澆置供應與冷縫風險」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Block placement needs continuous supply and orderly coverage. Insufficient delivery prolongs local intervals between layers, so meeting daily output does not establish acceptable continuity at every local interface. Assume block volume 600 m³ and effective supply 75 m³/h. Placement requires eight hours, or 9.5 h with a 1.5 h outage, excluding local compaction and coverage sequence. The same interruption produces different interface states at different temperatures, and adding water to restore workability changes material quality. Making up missing volume does not automatically remove an already formed weak layer. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Placement supply and cold joints” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設澆塊600 m³、有效供應率75 m³/h，純澆置需8 h；若停機1.5 h則9.5 h，未計振實和局部覆蓋順序。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume block volume 600 m³ and effective supply 75 m³/h.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要最後總澆置方量正確，局部冷縫就不會影響壩體。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Correct final placed volume means local cold joints cannot affect the dam.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「澆置供應與冷縫風險」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Placement supply and cold joints”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-05-k1","title":"澆置供應與冷縫風險","titleEn":"Placement supply and cold joints","text":"分塊澆築要求連續供料與有序覆蓋，供應率不足會延長新舊料接觸時間。總日產量達標不代表每一局部層面都在可接受條件下接續。","textEn":"Block placement needs continuous supply and orderly coverage. Insufficient delivery prolongs local intervals between layers, so meeting daily output does not establish acceptable continuity at every local interface.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要最後總澆置方量正確，局部冷縫就不會影響壩體。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Correct final placed volume means local cold joints cannot affect the dam. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「澆置供應與冷縫風險」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Placement supply and cold joints\" is correct?","options":["只要最後總澆置方量正確，局部冷縫就不會影響壩體。","接縫剪力能力可以直接等同完整混凝土的強度。","分塊澆築要求連續供料與有序覆蓋，供應率不足會延長新舊料接觸時間。"],"optionsEn":["Correct final placed volume means local cold joints cannot affect the dam.","A construction-joint shear capacity directly equals intact-concrete strength.","Block placement needs continuous supply and orderly coverage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"分塊澆築要求連續供料與有序覆蓋，供應率不足會延長新舊料接觸時間。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Block placement needs continuous supply and orderly coverage. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b231-v15-06","title":"澆置供應與冷縫風險：定量估算","titleEn":"Placement supply and cold joints: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「澆置供應與冷縫風險」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Placement supply and cold joints” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設澆塊600 m³、有效供應率75 m³/h，純澆置需8 h；若停機1.5 h則9.5 h，未計振實和局部覆蓋順序。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume block volume 600 m³ and effective supply 75 m³/h. Placement requires eight hours, or 9.5 h with a 1.5 h outage, excluding local compaction and coverage sequence. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：按位置記錄每批到達與覆蓋時間，對照氣溫、坍度與凝結資料；將供料停頓映射到實際層面，另以取芯或指定界面試驗檢查接續品質，而非只查總方量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record delivery and covering times by location and compare temperature, workability and setting data.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設澆塊600 m³、有效供應率75 m³/h，純澆置需8 h；若停機1.5 h則9.5 h，未計振實和局部覆蓋順序。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume block volume 600 m³ and effective supply 75 m³/h. Placement requires eight hours, or 9.5 h with a 1.5 h outage, excluding local compaction and coverage sequence.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「澆置供應與冷縫風險」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Placement supply and cold joints\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設澆塊600 m³、有效供應率75 m³/h，純澆置需8 h；若停機1.5 h則9.5 h，未計振實和局部覆蓋順序。","只要冷卻水流量夠大，便能保證混凝土沒有溫差裂縫。","接縫平均開度很小就能保證止水一定不會漏水。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume block volume 600 m³ and effective supply 75 m³/h.","Sufficiently high cooling-water flow guarantees freedom from thermal-gradient cracking.","A small mean joint opening guarantees that the waterstop cannot leak."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設澆塊600 m³、有效供應率75 m³/h，純澆置需8 h；若停機1.5 h則9.5 h，未計振實和局部覆蓋順序。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume block volume 600 m³ and effective supply 75 m³/h. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b231-v15-07","title":"澆置供應與冷縫風險：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Placement supply and cold joints: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「澆置供應與冷縫風險」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Placement supply and cold joints” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"按位置記錄每批到達與覆蓋時間，對照氣溫、坍度與凝結資料；將供料停頓映射到實際層面，另以取芯或指定界面試驗檢查接續品質，而非只查總方量。追蹤最久停頓位置的層面實際凝結狀況。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record delivery and covering times by location and compare temperature, workability and setting data. Map supply interruptions to actual interfaces, then examine joint quality with cores or specified interface tests rather than total volume alone. Track actual setting condition at the interface with the longest interruption. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以澆置供應與冷縫風險編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。按位置記錄每批到達與覆蓋時間，對照氣溫、坍度與凝結資料；將供料停頓映射到實際層面，另以取芯或指定界面試驗檢查接續品質，而非只查總方量。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for placement supply and cold joints, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Record delivery and covering times by location and compare temperature, workability and setting data. Map supply interruptions to actual interfaces, then examine joint quality with cores or specified interface tests rather than total volume alone.","failure":"注意干擾：同一停機時間在不同溫度下會產生不同接縫狀態，盲目加水恢復工作性又會改變材料品質。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: The same interruption produces different interface states at different temperatures, and adding water to restore workability changes material quality. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"按位置記錄每批到達與覆蓋時間，對照氣溫、坍度與凝結資料；將供料停頓映射到實際層面，另以取芯或指定界面試驗檢查接續品質，而非只查總方量。追蹤最久停頓位置的層面實際凝結狀況。","textEn":"Record delivery and covering times by location and compare temperature, workability and setting data. Map supply interruptions to actual interfaces, then examine joint quality with cores or specified interface tests rather than total volume alone. Track actual setting condition at the interface with the longest interruption.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以澆置供應與冷縫風險編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。按位置記錄每批到達與覆蓋時間，對照氣溫、坍度與凝結資料；將供料停頓映射到實際層面，另以取芯或指定界面試驗檢查接續品質，而非只查總方量。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for placement supply and cold joints, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Record delivery and covering times by location and compare temperature, workability and setting data. Map supply interruptions to actual interfaces, then examine joint quality with cores or specified interface tests rather than total volume alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「澆置供應與冷縫風險」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Placement supply and cold joints\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","按位置記錄每批到達與覆蓋時間，對照氣溫、坍度與凝結資料；將供料停頓映射到實際層面，另以取芯或指定界面試驗檢查接續品質，而非只查總方量。","圖面有排水孔就能不量孔壓而忽略全部基底上浮。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Record delivery and covering times by location and compare temperature, workability and setting data.","Drains shown on drawings allow all foundation uplift to be ignored without pressure measurements."],"answer":1,"explanation":"按位置記錄每批到達與覆蓋時間，對照氣溫、坍度與凝結資料；將供料停頓映射到實際層面，另以取芯或指定界面試驗檢查接續品質，而非只查總方量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record delivery and covering times by location and compare temperature, workability and setting data. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b231-v15-08","title":"澆置供應與冷縫風險：失效診斷","titleEn":"Placement supply and cold joints: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「澆置供應與冷縫風險」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Placement supply and cold joints” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"同一停機時間在不同溫度下會產生不同接縫狀態，盲目加水恢復工作性又會改變材料品質。若只補足少澆的方量，已形成的弱層不會自動消失。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"The same interruption produces different interface states at different temperatures, and adding water to restore workability changes material quality. Making up missing volume does not automatically remove an already formed weak layer. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若只補足少澆的方量，已形成的弱層不會自動消失。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Making up missing volume does not automatically remove an already formed weak layer.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要最後總澆置方量正確，局部冷縫就不會影響壩體。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Correct final placed volume means local cold joints cannot affect the dam.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"同一停機時間在不同溫度下會產生不同接縫狀態，盲目加水恢復工作性又會改變材料品質。若只補足少澆的方量，已形成的弱層不會自動消失。","textEn":"The same interruption produces different interface states at different temperatures, and adding water to restore workability changes material quality. Making up missing volume does not automatically remove an already formed weak layer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「澆置供應與冷縫風險」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Placement supply and cold joints\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","接縫剪力能力可以直接等同完整混凝土的強度。","同一停機時間在不同溫度下會產生不同接縫狀態，盲目加水恢復工作性又會改變材料品質。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A construction-joint shear capacity directly equals intact-concrete strength.","The same interruption produces different interface states at different temperatures, and adding water to restore workability changes material quality."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同一停機時間在不同溫度下會產生不同接縫狀態，盲目加水恢復工作性又會改變材料品質。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"The same interruption produces different interface states at different temperatures, and adding water to restore workability changes material quality. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b231-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「層面剪力與有效正應力」與「熱擴散與澆塊尺寸」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Lift-joint shear and effective stress\" and \"Thermal diffusion and block dimensions\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b231-v15-09","title":"層面剪力與有效正應力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Lift-joint shear and effective stress: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「層面剪力與有效正應力」如何影響混凝土重力壩分塊澆築的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Lift-joint shear and effective stress” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Block-by-block concrete gravity-dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水平施工層面傳遞剪力，黏聚、摩擦與孔壓共同控制可動員阻力。層面清理和骨材嵌固影響黏結，不能用完整混凝土強度直接代表接縫。 假設層面面積100 m²、總正力30 MN、上浮10 MN、c=0.1 MPa、μ=0.6，阻力cA+μ(N−U)=22 MN；參數為假設峰值。 漿皮或污染使層面黏結降低，孔壓增加又削弱摩擦項。若在可能開裂的接縫仍無條件保留黏聚力，會高估滑動後阻力並掩蓋排水功能的重要性。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「層面剪力與有效正應力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Horizontal lift joints transfer shear through cohesion and friction under effective normal stress. Cleaning and aggregate interlock affect bond, so intact-concrete strength cannot directly represent the interface. Assume interface area 100 m², normal force 30 MN, uplift 10 MN, c=0.1 MPa and μ=0.6. Resistance cA+μ(N−U)=22 MN, using assumed peak parameters. Laitance or contamination reduces bond, while pore pressure reduces friction. Retaining cohesion unconditionally after possible cracking overstates post-movement resistance and obscures the importance of drainage performance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Lift-joint shear and effective stress” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設層面面積100 m²、總正力30 MN、上浮10 MN、c=0.1 MPa、μ=0.6，阻力cA+μ(N−U)=22 MN；參數為假設峰值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume interface area 100 m², normal force 30 MN, uplift 10 MN, c=0.1 MPa and μ=0.6.","failure":"常見誤解：「接縫剪力能力可以直接等同完整混凝土的強度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A construction-joint shear capacity directly equals intact-concrete strength.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「層面剪力與有效正應力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Lift-joint shear and effective stress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-09-k1","title":"層面剪力與有效正應力","titleEn":"Lift-joint shear and effective stress","text":"水平施工層面傳遞剪力，黏聚、摩擦與孔壓共同控制可動員阻力。層面清理和骨材嵌固影響黏結，不能用完整混凝土強度直接代表接縫。","textEn":"Horizontal lift joints transfer shear through cohesion and friction under effective normal stress. Cleaning and aggregate interlock affect bond, so intact-concrete strength cannot directly represent the interface.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：接縫剪力能力可以直接等同完整混凝土的強度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A construction-joint shear capacity directly equals intact-concrete strength. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「層面剪力與有效正應力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Lift-joint shear and effective stress\" is correct?","options":["水平施工層面傳遞剪力，黏聚、摩擦與孔壓共同控制可動員阻力。","接縫剪力能力可以直接等同完整混凝土的強度。","澆塊厚度加倍只會讓熱擴散時間加倍。"],"optionsEn":["Horizontal lift joints transfer shear through cohesion and friction under effective normal stress.","A construction-joint shear capacity directly equals intact-concrete strength.","Doubling block thickness only doubles the thermal diffusion time."],"answer":0,"explanation":"水平施工層面傳遞剪力，黏聚、摩擦與孔壓共同控制可動員阻力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Horizontal lift joints transfer shear through cohesion and friction under effective normal stress. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b231-v15-10","title":"層面剪力與有效正應力：定量估算","titleEn":"Lift-joint shear and effective stress: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「層面剪力與有效正應力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Lift-joint shear and effective stress” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設層面面積100 m²、總正力30 MN、上浮10 MN、c=0.1 MPa、μ=0.6，阻力cA+μ(N−U)=22 MN；參數為假設峰值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume interface area 100 m², normal force 30 MN, uplift 10 MN, c=0.1 MPa and μ=0.6. Resistance cA+μ(N−U)=22 MN, using assumed peak parameters. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以層面取芯與剪切試驗核對黏結及粗糙度，將孔壓測站換算到相同層位；分列峰值與殘餘參數，檢查抗力式是否對應實際可用接觸面積。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check bond and roughness with interface cores and shear testing, referring piezometers to the same lift.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設層面面積100 m²、總正力30 MN、上浮10 MN、c=0.1 MPa、μ=0.6，阻力cA+μ(N−U)=22 MN；參數為假設峰值。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume interface area 100 m², normal force 30 MN, uplift 10 MN, c=0.1 MPa and μ=0.6. Resistance cA+μ(N−U)=22 MN, using assumed peak parameters.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「層面剪力與有效正應力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Lift-joint shear and effective stress\", which statement holds?","options":["成熟度達到固定數字就代表所有混凝土具有同一強度。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設層面面積100 m²、總正力30 MN、上浮10 MN、c=0.1 MPa、μ=0.6，阻力cA+μ(N−U)=22 MN。","混凝土剛澆入就已完全自立，所以模板不承受液態側壓。"],"optionsEn":["A fixed maturity value means every concrete mixture has the same strength.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume interface area 100 m², normal force 30 MN, uplift 10 MN, c=0.1 MPa and μ=0.6.","Freshly placed concrete is immediately self-supporting and exerts no fluid-like form pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設層面面積100 m²、總正力30 MN、上浮10 MN、c=0.1 MPa、μ=0.6，阻力cA+μ(N−U)=22 MN；參數為假設峰值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume interface area 100 m², normal force 30 MN, uplift 10 MN, c=0.1 MPa and μ=0.6. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b231-v15-11","title":"層面剪力與有效正應力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Lift-joint shear and effective stress: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「層面剪力與有效正應力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Lift-joint shear and effective stress” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以層面取芯與剪切試驗核對黏結及粗糙度，將孔壓測站換算到相同層位；分列峰值與殘餘參數，檢查抗力式是否對應實際可用接觸面積。以滑移後試驗檢查是否仍可保留黏聚項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check bond and roughness with interface cores and shear testing, referring piezometers to the same lift. Separate peak and residual parameters and verify that the resistance formula uses the actual available contact area. Use post-slip testing to check whether retaining cohesion remains defensible. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以層面剪力與有效正應力編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。以層面取芯與剪切試驗核對黏結及粗糙度，將孔壓測站換算到相同層位；分列峰值與殘餘參數，檢查抗力式是否對應實際可用接觸面積。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for lift-joint shear and effective stress, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Check bond and roughness with interface cores and shear testing, referring piezometers to the same lift. Separate peak and residual parameters and verify that the resistance formula uses the actual available contact area.","failure":"注意干擾：漿皮或污染使層面黏結降低，孔壓增加又削弱摩擦項。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Laitance or contamination reduces bond, while pore pressure reduces friction. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以層面取芯與剪切試驗核對黏結及粗糙度，將孔壓測站換算到相同層位；分列峰值與殘餘參數，檢查抗力式是否對應實際可用接觸面積。以滑移後試驗檢查是否仍可保留黏聚項。","textEn":"Check bond and roughness with interface cores and shear testing, referring piezometers to the same lift. Separate peak and residual parameters and verify that the resistance formula uses the actual available contact area. Use post-slip testing to check whether retaining cohesion remains defensible.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以層面剪力與有效正應力編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。以層面取芯與剪切試驗核對黏結及粗糙度，將孔壓測站換算到相同層位；分列峰值與殘餘參數，檢查抗力式是否對應實際可用接觸面積。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for lift-joint shear and effective stress, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Check bond and roughness with interface cores and shear testing, referring piezometers to the same lift. Separate peak and residual parameters and verify that the resistance formula uses the actual available contact area.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「層面剪力與有效正應力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Lift-joint shear and effective stress\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","進料總方量與設計相符就能證明澆塊內完全沒有缺陷。","以層面取芯與剪切試驗核對黏結及粗糙度，將孔壓測站換算到相同層位；分列峰值與殘餘參數，檢查抗力式是否對應實際可用接觸面積。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Matching delivered and design volume proves the entire block is defect-free.","Check bond and roughness with interface cores and shear testing, referring piezometers to the same lift."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以層面取芯與剪切試驗核對黏結及粗糙度，將孔壓測站換算到相同層位；分列峰值與殘餘參數，檢查抗力式是否對應實際可用接觸面積。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check bond and roughness with interface cores and shear testing, referring piezometers to the same lift. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b231-v15-12","title":"層面剪力與有效正應力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Lift-joint shear and effective stress: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「層面剪力與有效正應力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Lift-joint shear and effective stress” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"漿皮或污染使層面黏結降低，孔壓增加又削弱摩擦項。若在可能開裂的接縫仍無條件保留黏聚力，會高估滑動後阻力並掩蓋排水功能的重要性。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Laitance or contamination reduces bond, while pore pressure reduces friction. Retaining cohesion unconditionally after possible cracking overstates post-movement resistance and obscures the importance of drainage performance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若在可能開裂的接縫仍無條件保留黏聚力，會高估滑動後阻力並掩蓋排水功能的重要性。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Retaining cohesion unconditionally after possible cracking overstates post-movement resistance and obscures the importance of drainage performance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「接縫剪力能力可以直接等同完整混凝土的強度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A construction-joint shear capacity directly equals intact-concrete strength.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"漿皮或污染使層面黏結降低，孔壓增加又削弱摩擦項。若在可能開裂的接縫仍無條件保留黏聚力，會高估滑動後阻力並掩蓋排水功能的重要性。","textEn":"Laitance or contamination reduces bond, while pore pressure reduces friction. Retaining cohesion unconditionally after possible cracking overstates post-movement resistance and obscures the importance of drainage performance.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「層面剪力與有效正應力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Lift-joint shear and effective stress\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["漿皮或污染使層面黏結降低，孔壓增加又削弱摩擦項。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","澆塊厚度加倍只會讓熱擴散時間加倍。"],"optionsEn":["Laitance or contamination reduces bond, while pore pressure reduces friction.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Doubling block thickness only doubles the thermal diffusion time."],"answer":0,"explanation":"漿皮或污染使層面黏結降低，孔壓增加又削弱摩擦項。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Laitance or contamination reduces bond, while pore pressure reduces friction. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b231-v15-13","title":"熱擴散與澆塊尺寸：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Thermal diffusion and block dimensions: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「熱擴散與澆塊尺寸」如何影響混凝土重力壩分塊澆築的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Thermal diffusion and block dimensions” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Block-by-block concrete gravity-dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"熱擴散時間大致與傳熱距離平方成正比，澆塊尺度增加會讓中心維持高溫更久。這個尺度關係說明分塊原因，但不能給出精確冷卻完成時間。 假設熱擴散係數α=10⁻⁶ m²/s、特徵距離2 m，t=L²/α=4 million s=46.30 days；僅尺度估算，不是指定等待期。 用半厚或全厚當距離會造成四倍時間差，必須與邊界定義一致。後續澆層改變表面散熱條件，原本冷卻中的塊體可能再升溫，不能只外推初期曲線。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「熱擴散與澆塊尺寸」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Thermal diffusion time scales approximately with the square of travel distance, so larger blocks retain core heat longer. This explains the value of subdivision without predicting an exact cooling-completion time. Assume diffusivity α=10⁻⁶ m²/s and characteristic distance 2 m. t=L²/α=4 million s=46.30 days, a scale estimate rather than a prescribed waiting period. Using half-thickness versus full thickness changes the time scale fourfold and must match boundary definitions. Later lifts alter heat loss and can reheat a cooling block, invalidating simple extrapolation of early records. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Thermal diffusion and block dimensions” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設熱擴散係數α=10⁻⁶ m²/s、特徵距離2 m，t=L²/α=4 million s=46.30 days；僅尺度估算，不是指定等待期。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume diffusivity α=10⁻⁶ m²/s and characteristic distance 2 m. t=L²/α=4 million s=46.30 days, a scale estimate rather than a prescribed waiting period.","failure":"常見誤解：「澆塊厚度加倍只會讓熱擴散時間加倍。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Doubling block thickness only doubles the thermal diffusion time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「熱擴散與澆塊尺寸」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Thermal diffusion and block dimensions”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-13-k1","title":"熱擴散與澆塊尺寸","titleEn":"Thermal diffusion and block dimensions","text":"熱擴散時間大致與傳熱距離平方成正比，澆塊尺度增加會讓中心維持高溫更久。這個尺度關係說明分塊原因，但不能給出精確冷卻完成時間。","textEn":"Thermal diffusion time scales approximately with the square of travel distance, so larger blocks retain core heat longer. This explains the value of subdivision without predicting an exact cooling-completion time.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：澆塊厚度加倍只會讓熱擴散時間加倍。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Doubling block thickness only doubles the thermal diffusion time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「熱擴散與澆塊尺寸」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Thermal diffusion and block dimensions\" is correct?","options":["澆塊厚度加倍只會讓熱擴散時間加倍。","熱擴散時間大致與傳熱距離平方成正比，澆塊尺度增加會讓中心維持高溫更久。","只要冷卻水流量夠大，便能保證混凝土沒有溫差裂縫。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling block thickness only doubles the thermal diffusion time.","Thermal diffusion time scales approximately with the square of travel distance, so larger blocks retain core heat longer.","Sufficiently high cooling-water flow guarantees freedom from thermal-gradient cracking."],"answer":1,"explanation":"熱擴散時間大致與傳熱距離平方成正比，澆塊尺度增加會讓中心維持高溫更久。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Thermal diffusion time scales approximately with the square of travel distance, so larger blocks retain core heat longer. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b231-v15-14","title":"熱擴散與澆塊尺寸：定量估算","titleEn":"Thermal diffusion and block dimensions: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「熱擴散與澆塊尺寸」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Thermal diffusion and block dimensions” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設熱擴散係數α=10⁻⁶ m²/s、特徵距離2 m，t=L²/α=4 million s=46.30 days；僅尺度估算，不是指定等待期。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume diffusivity α=10⁻⁶ m²/s and characteristic distance 2 m. t=L²/α=4 million s=46.30 days, a scale estimate rather than a prescribed waiting period. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較不同深度溫度變化的相位與幅度，以實測材料導熱率和熱容量重建擴散係數；將冷卻管、表面邊界和新增澆層列入，檢查單一距離是否具代表性。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare temperature phase and amplitude at several depths and derive diffusivity from measured conductivity and heat capacity.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設熱擴散係數α=10⁻⁶ m²/s、特徵距離2 m，t=L²/α=4 million s=46.30 days；僅尺度估算，不是指定等待期。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume diffusivity α=10⁻⁶ m²/s and characteristic distance 2 m. t=L²/α=4 million s=46.30 days, a scale estimate rather than a prescribed waiting period.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「熱擴散與澆塊尺寸」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Thermal diffusion and block dimensions\", which statement holds?","options":["接縫平均開度很小就能保證止水一定不會漏水。","圖面有排水孔就能不量孔壓而忽略全部基底上浮。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設熱擴散係數α=10⁻⁶ m²/s、特徵距離2 m，t=L²/α=4 million s=46.30 days。"],"optionsEn":["A small mean joint opening guarantees that the waterstop cannot leak.","Drains shown on drawings allow all foundation uplift to be ignored without pressure measurements.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume diffusivity α=10⁻⁶ m²/s and characteristic distance 2 m. t=L²/α=4 million s=46.30 days, a scale estimate rather than a prescribed waiting period."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設熱擴散係數α=10⁻⁶ m²/s、特徵距離2 m，t=L²/α=4 million s=46.30 days；僅尺度估算，不是指定等待期。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume diffusivity α=10⁻⁶ m²/s and characteristic distance 2 m. t=L²/α=4 million s=46.30 days, a scale estimate rather than a prescribed waiting period. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b231-v15-15","title":"熱擴散與澆塊尺寸：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Thermal diffusion and block dimensions: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「熱擴散與澆塊尺寸」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Thermal diffusion and block dimensions” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較不同深度溫度變化的相位與幅度，以實測材料導熱率和熱容量重建擴散係數；將冷卻管、表面邊界和新增澆層列入，檢查單一距離是否具代表性。比較半厚與全厚邊界定義對時間尺度的影響。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare temperature phase and amplitude at several depths and derive diffusivity from measured conductivity and heat capacity. Include cooling pipes, surface conditions and added lifts, testing whether one characteristic distance is representative. Compare half-thickness and full-thickness boundary definitions in the diffusion scale. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以熱擴散與澆塊尺寸編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。比較不同深度溫度變化的相位與幅度，以實測材料導熱率和熱容量重建擴散係數；將冷卻管、表面邊界和新增澆層列入，檢查單一距離是否具代表性。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for thermal diffusion and block dimensions, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare temperature phase and amplitude at several depths and derive diffusivity from measured conductivity and heat capacity. Include cooling pipes, surface conditions and added lifts, testing whether one characteristic distance is representative.","failure":"注意干擾：用半厚或全厚當距離會造成四倍時間差，必須與邊界定義一致。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using half-thickness versus full thickness changes the time scale fourfold and must match boundary definitions. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較不同深度溫度變化的相位與幅度，以實測材料導熱率和熱容量重建擴散係數；將冷卻管、表面邊界和新增澆層列入，檢查單一距離是否具代表性。比較半厚與全厚邊界定義對時間尺度的影響。","textEn":"Compare temperature phase and amplitude at several depths and derive diffusivity from measured conductivity and heat capacity. Include cooling pipes, surface conditions and added lifts, testing whether one characteristic distance is representative. Compare half-thickness and full-thickness boundary definitions in the diffusion scale.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以熱擴散與澆塊尺寸編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。比較不同深度溫度變化的相位與幅度，以實測材料導熱率和熱容量重建擴散係數；將冷卻管、表面邊界和新增澆層列入，檢查單一距離是否具代表性。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for thermal diffusion and block dimensions, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare temperature phase and amplitude at several depths and derive diffusivity from measured conductivity and heat capacity. Include cooling pipes, surface conditions and added lifts, testing whether one characteristic distance is representative.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「熱擴散與澆塊尺寸」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Thermal diffusion and block dimensions\"?","options":["比較不同深度溫度變化的相位與幅度，以實測材料導熱率和熱容量重建擴散係數；將冷卻管、表面邊界和新增澆層列入，檢查單一距離是否具代表性。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","絕熱溫升就是工地澆塊必定量到的最高溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Compare temperature phase and amplitude at several depths and derive diffusivity from measured conductivity and heat capacity.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Adiabatic temperature rise is the highest temperature that every placed block must reach."],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較不同深度溫度變化的相位與幅度，以實測材料導熱率和熱容量重建擴散係數；將冷卻管、表面邊界和新增澆層列入，檢查單一距離是否具代表性。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare temperature phase and amplitude at several depths and derive diffusivity from measured conductivity and heat capacity. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b231-v15-16","title":"熱擴散與澆塊尺寸：失效診斷","titleEn":"Thermal diffusion and block dimensions: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「熱擴散與澆塊尺寸」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Thermal diffusion and block dimensions” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用半厚或全厚當距離會造成四倍時間差，必須與邊界定義一致。後續澆層改變表面散熱條件，原本冷卻中的塊體可能再升溫，不能只外推初期曲線。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using half-thickness versus full thickness changes the time scale fourfold and must match boundary definitions. Later lifts alter heat loss and can reheat a cooling block, invalidating simple extrapolation of early records. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：後續澆層改變表面散熱條件，原本冷卻中的塊體可能再升溫，不能只外推初期曲線。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Later lifts alter heat loss and can reheat a cooling block, invalidating simple extrapolation of early records.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「澆塊厚度加倍只會讓熱擴散時間加倍。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Doubling block thickness only doubles the thermal diffusion time.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用半厚或全厚當距離會造成四倍時間差，必須與邊界定義一致。後續澆層改變表面散熱條件，原本冷卻中的塊體可能再升溫，不能只外推初期曲線。","textEn":"Using half-thickness versus full thickness changes the time scale fourfold and must match boundary definitions. Later lifts alter heat loss and can reheat a cooling block, invalidating simple extrapolation of early records.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱擴散與澆塊尺寸」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Thermal diffusion and block dimensions\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","用半厚或全厚當距離會造成四倍時間差，必須與邊界定義一致。","只要冷卻水流量夠大，便能保證混凝土沒有溫差裂縫。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Using half-thickness versus full thickness changes the time scale fourfold and must match boundary definitions.","Sufficiently high cooling-water flow guarantees freedom from thermal-gradient cracking."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用半厚或全厚當距離會造成四倍時間差，必須與邊界定義一致。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using half-thickness versus full thickness changes the time scale fourfold and must match boundary definitions. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b231-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「冷卻水能量移除」與「成熟度與強度校正」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Cooling-water heat removal\" and \"Maturity and strength calibration\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b231-v15-17","title":"冷卻水能量移除：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cooling-water heat removal: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「冷卻水能量移除」如何影響混凝土重力壩分塊澆築的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cooling-water heat removal” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Block-by-block concrete gravity-dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"埋管冷卻以水流帶走熱量，進出口溫差與流量共同決定移熱率。大流量低溫差和小流量高溫差不能只憑其中一項判斷效果。 假設水流2 kg/s、比熱4.18 kJ/(kg·K)、升溫5 K，移熱率41.8 kW；持續24 h移除3.61152 GJ，忽略流量溫差變化。 冷卻過快可能加大局部溫差和拉應力，不是移熱越多就越好。進出口感測器零點差也會在小溫差時造成大比例誤差，掩蓋實際冷卻不足。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「冷卻水能量移除」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Embedded cooling removes heat through water flow, with inlet-outlet temperature difference and flow jointly determining removal. Neither flow nor temperature rise alone establishes cooling performance. Assume water flow 2 kg/s, heat capacity 4.18 kJ/(kg·K) and rise 5 K. Heat removal is 41.8 kW or 3.61152 GJ over 24 h at constant conditions. Excessively fast cooling increases local gradients and tension, so more heat removal is not always better. Sensor offset between inlet and outlet causes large relative errors at small differences and can conceal inadequate removal. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cooling-water heat removal” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設水流2 kg/s、比熱4.18 kJ/(kg·K)、升溫5 K，移熱率41.8 kW；持續24 h移除3.61152 GJ，忽略流量溫差變化。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume water flow 2 kg/s, heat capacity 4.18 kJ/(kg·K) and rise 5 K.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要冷卻水流量夠大，便能保證混凝土沒有溫差裂縫。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Sufficiently high cooling-water flow guarantees freedom from thermal-gradient cracking.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「冷卻水能量移除」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cooling-water heat removal”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-17-k1","title":"冷卻水能量移除","titleEn":"Cooling-water heat removal","text":"埋管冷卻以水流帶走熱量，進出口溫差與流量共同決定移熱率。大流量低溫差和小流量高溫差不能只憑其中一項判斷效果。","textEn":"Embedded cooling removes heat through water flow, with inlet-outlet temperature difference and flow jointly determining removal. Neither flow nor temperature rise alone establishes cooling performance.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要冷卻水流量夠大，便能保證混凝土沒有溫差裂縫。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Sufficiently high cooling-water flow guarantees freedom from thermal-gradient cracking. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「冷卻水能量移除」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cooling-water heat removal\" is correct?","options":["只要冷卻水流量夠大，便能保證混凝土沒有溫差裂縫。","成熟度達到固定數字就代表所有混凝土具有同一強度。","埋管冷卻以水流帶走熱量，進出口溫差與流量共同決定移熱率。"],"optionsEn":["Sufficiently high cooling-water flow guarantees freedom from thermal-gradient cracking.","A fixed maturity value means every concrete mixture has the same strength.","Embedded cooling removes heat through water flow, with inlet-outlet temperature difference and flow jointly determining removal."],"answer":2,"explanation":"埋管冷卻以水流帶走熱量，進出口溫差與流量共同決定移熱率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Embedded cooling removes heat through water flow, with inlet-outlet temperature difference and flow jointly determining removal. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b231-v15-18","title":"冷卻水能量移除：定量估算","titleEn":"Cooling-water heat removal: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「冷卻水能量移除」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cooling-water heat removal” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設水流2 kg/s、比熱4.18 kJ/(kg·K)、升溫5 K，移熱率41.8 kW；持續24 h移除3.61152 GJ，忽略流量溫差變化。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume water flow 2 kg/s, heat capacity 4.18 kJ/(kg·K) and rise 5 K. Heat removal is 41.8 kW or 3.61152 GJ over 24 h at constant conditions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步量測各迴路進出口溫度和流量，積分移熱量與壩內溫度下降比較；檢查旁通、儀器偏差與管路漏水，避免只以泵流量代替真正穿過埋管的流量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure temperature and flow in each circuit synchronously and compare integrated removal with internal cooling.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設水流2 kg/s、比熱4.18 kJ/(kg·K)、升溫5 K，移熱率41.8 kW；持續24 h移除3.61152 GJ，忽略流量溫差變化。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume water flow 2 kg/s, heat capacity 4.18 kJ/(kg·K) and rise 5 K. Heat removal is 41.8 kW or 3.61152 GJ over 24 h at constant conditions.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「冷卻水能量移除」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cooling-water heat removal\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設水流2 kg/s、比熱4.18 kJ/(kg·K)、升溫5 K，移熱率41.8 kW。","混凝土剛澆入就已完全自立，所以模板不承受液態側壓。","進料總方量與設計相符就能證明澆塊內完全沒有缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume water flow 2 kg/s, heat capacity 4.18 kJ/(kg·K) and rise 5 K.","Freshly placed concrete is immediately self-supporting and exerts no fluid-like form pressure.","Matching delivered and design volume proves the entire block is defect-free."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設水流2 kg/s、比熱4.18 kJ/(kg·K)、升溫5 K，移熱率41.8 kW；持續24 h移除3.61152 GJ，忽略流量溫差變化。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume water flow 2 kg/s, heat capacity 4.18 kJ/(kg·K) and rise 5 K. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b231-v15-19","title":"冷卻水能量移除：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cooling-water heat removal: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「冷卻水能量移除」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cooling-water heat removal” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步量測各迴路進出口溫度和流量，積分移熱量與壩內溫度下降比較；檢查旁通、儀器偏差與管路漏水，避免只以泵流量代替真正穿過埋管的流量。以分迴路熱量總和檢查主回水量測的閉合。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure temperature and flow in each circuit synchronously and compare integrated removal with internal cooling. Check bypasses, instrument bias and leaks instead of using pump discharge as the flow through embedded pipes. Check main-return measurements against the sum of individual circuit heat removal. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以冷卻水能量移除編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。同步量測各迴路進出口溫度和流量，積分移熱量與壩內溫度下降比較；檢查旁通、儀器偏差與管路漏水，避免只以泵流量代替真正穿過埋管的流量。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for cooling-water heat removal, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Measure temperature and flow in each circuit synchronously and compare integrated removal with internal cooling. Check bypasses, instrument bias and leaks instead of using pump discharge as the flow through embedded pipes.","failure":"注意干擾：冷卻過快可能加大局部溫差和拉應力，不是移熱越多就越好。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Excessively fast cooling increases local gradients and tension, so more heat removal is not always better. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步量測各迴路進出口溫度和流量，積分移熱量與壩內溫度下降比較；檢查旁通、儀器偏差與管路漏水，避免只以泵流量代替真正穿過埋管的流量。以分迴路熱量總和檢查主回水量測的閉合。","textEn":"Measure temperature and flow in each circuit synchronously and compare integrated removal with internal cooling. Check bypasses, instrument bias and leaks instead of using pump discharge as the flow through embedded pipes. Check main-return measurements against the sum of individual circuit heat removal.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以冷卻水能量移除編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。同步量測各迴路進出口溫度和流量，積分移熱量與壩內溫度下降比較；檢查旁通、儀器偏差與管路漏水，避免只以泵流量代替真正穿過埋管的流量。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for cooling-water heat removal, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Measure temperature and flow in each circuit synchronously and compare integrated removal with internal cooling. Check bypasses, instrument bias and leaks instead of using pump discharge as the flow through embedded pipes.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「冷卻水能量移除」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cooling-water heat removal\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","同步量測各迴路進出口溫度和流量，積分移熱量與壩內溫度下降比較；檢查旁通、儀器偏差與管路漏水，避免只以泵流量代替真正穿過埋管的流量。","只要最後總澆置方量正確，局部冷縫就不會影響壩體。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Measure temperature and flow in each circuit synchronously and compare integrated removal with internal cooling.","Correct final placed volume means local cold joints cannot affect the dam."],"answer":1,"explanation":"同步量測各迴路進出口溫度和流量，積分移熱量與壩內溫度下降比較；檢查旁通、儀器偏差與管路漏水，避免只以泵流量代替真正穿過埋管的流量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure temperature and flow in each circuit synchronously and compare integrated removal with internal cooling. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b231-v15-20","title":"冷卻水能量移除：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cooling-water heat removal: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「冷卻水能量移除」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cooling-water heat removal” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"冷卻過快可能加大局部溫差和拉應力，不是移熱越多就越好。進出口感測器零點差也會在小溫差時造成大比例誤差，掩蓋實際冷卻不足。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Excessively fast cooling increases local gradients and tension, so more heat removal is not always better. Sensor offset between inlet and outlet causes large relative errors at small differences and can conceal inadequate removal. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：進出口感測器零點差也會在小溫差時造成大比例誤差，掩蓋實際冷卻不足。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Sensor offset between inlet and outlet causes large relative errors at small differences and can conceal inadequate removal.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要冷卻水流量夠大，便能保證混凝土沒有溫差裂縫。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Sufficiently high cooling-water flow guarantees freedom from thermal-gradient cracking.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"冷卻過快可能加大局部溫差和拉應力，不是移熱越多就越好。進出口感測器零點差也會在小溫差時造成大比例誤差，掩蓋實際冷卻不足。","textEn":"Excessively fast cooling increases local gradients and tension, so more heat removal is not always better. Sensor offset between inlet and outlet causes large relative errors at small differences and can conceal inadequate removal.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「冷卻水能量移除」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cooling-water heat removal\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","成熟度達到固定數字就代表所有混凝土具有同一強度。","冷卻過快可能加大局部溫差和拉應力，不是移熱越多就越好。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A fixed maturity value means every concrete mixture has the same strength.","Excessively fast cooling increases local gradients and tension, so more heat removal is not always better."],"answer":2,"explanation":"冷卻過快可能加大局部溫差和拉應力，不是移熱越多就越好。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Excessively fast cooling increases local gradients and tension, so more heat removal is not always better. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b231-v15-21","title":"成熟度與強度校正：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Maturity and strength calibration: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「成熟度與強度校正」如何影響混凝土重力壩分塊澆築的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Maturity and strength calibration” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Block-by-block concrete gravity-dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"成熟度把時間和溫度整合為水化歷程指標，必須經同配比強度校正才可推論能力。不同膠結材或養護濕度會改變關係，不能把成熟度當直接強度。 假設Nurse-Saul基準溫度−10°C，混凝土20°C維持48 h，M=(20−(−10))×48=1440°C·h；未由此指定任何MPa。 高早期溫度可能改變後期強度發展，乾燥也可能中斷水化。若以其他配方成熟度曲線套用，會產生看似精確但缺乏材料依據的承載判讀。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「成熟度與強度校正」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Maturity combines time and temperature into a hydration-history index and needs same-mixture calibration before implying strength. Binder and curing moisture change the relationship, so maturity is not strength itself. Assume Nurse-Saul datum −10°C and concrete at 20°C for 48 h. M=(20−(−10))×48=1440°C·h, without assigning any strength in MPa. High early temperature can alter later strength development, and drying can interrupt hydration. Borrowing another mixture maturity curve creates apparently precise capacity estimates without the required material-specific evidence. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Maturity and strength calibration” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設Nurse-Saul基準溫度−10°C，混凝土20°C維持48 h，M=(20−(−10))×48=1440°C·h；未由此指定任何MPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume Nurse-Saul datum −10°C and concrete at 20°C for 48 h.","failure":"常見誤解：「成熟度達到固定數字就代表所有混凝土具有同一強度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A fixed maturity value means every concrete mixture has the same strength.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「成熟度與強度校正」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Maturity and strength calibration”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-21-k1","title":"成熟度與強度校正","titleEn":"Maturity and strength calibration","text":"成熟度把時間和溫度整合為水化歷程指標，必須經同配比強度校正才可推論能力。不同膠結材或養護濕度會改變關係，不能把成熟度當直接強度。","textEn":"Maturity combines time and temperature into a hydration-history index and needs same-mixture calibration before implying strength. Binder and curing moisture change the relationship, so maturity is not strength itself.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：成熟度達到固定數字就代表所有混凝土具有同一強度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A fixed maturity value means every concrete mixture has the same strength. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「成熟度與強度校正」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Maturity and strength calibration\" is correct?","options":["成熟度把時間和溫度整合為水化歷程指標，必須經同配比強度校正才可推論能力。","成熟度達到固定數字就代表所有混凝土具有同一強度。","接縫平均開度很小就能保證止水一定不會漏水。"],"optionsEn":["Maturity combines time and temperature into a hydration-history index and needs same-mixture calibration before implying strength.","A fixed maturity value means every concrete mixture has the same strength.","A small mean joint opening guarantees that the waterstop cannot leak."],"answer":0,"explanation":"成熟度把時間和溫度整合為水化歷程指標，必須經同配比強度校正才可推論能力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Maturity combines time and temperature into a hydration-history index and needs same-mixture calibration before implying strength. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b231-v15-22","title":"成熟度與強度校正：定量估算","titleEn":"Maturity and strength calibration: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「成熟度與強度校正」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Maturity and strength calibration” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設Nurse-Saul基準溫度−10°C，混凝土20°C維持48 h，M=(20−(−10))×48=1440°C·h；未由此指定任何MPa。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume Nurse-Saul datum −10°C and concrete at 20°C for 48 h. M=(20−(−10))×48=1440°C·h, without assigning any strength in MPa. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用現場溫度歷線積分而非平均氣溫，與同配比不同齡期試體建立關係；另核對濕養護和高溫歷程是否超出校正範圍，保留實際拉壓強度試驗。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Integrate concrete temperature histories rather than ambient averages and calibrate with same-mixture specimens of different ages.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設Nurse-Saul基準溫度−10°C，混凝土20°C維持48 h，M=(20−(−10))×48=1440°C·h；未由此指定任何MPa。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume Nurse-Saul datum −10°C and concrete at 20°C for 48 h. M=(20−(−10))×48=1440°C·h, without assigning any strength in MPa.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「成熟度與強度校正」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Maturity and strength calibration\", which statement holds?","options":["圖面有排水孔就能不量孔壓而忽略全部基底上浮。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設Nurse-Saul基準溫度−10°C，混凝土20°C維持48 h，M=(20−(−10))×48=1440°C·h。","絕熱溫升就是工地澆塊必定量到的最高溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Drains shown on drawings allow all foundation uplift to be ignored without pressure measurements.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume Nurse-Saul datum −10°C and concrete at 20°C for 48 h.","Adiabatic temperature rise is the highest temperature that every placed block must reach."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設Nurse-Saul基準溫度−10°C，混凝土20°C維持48 h，M=(20−(−10))×48=1440°C·h；未由此指定任何MPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume Nurse-Saul datum −10°C and concrete at 20°C for 48 h. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b231-v15-23","title":"成熟度與強度校正：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Maturity and strength calibration: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「成熟度與強度校正」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Maturity and strength calibration” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用現場溫度歷線積分而非平均氣溫，與同配比不同齡期試體建立關係；另核對濕養護和高溫歷程是否超出校正範圍，保留實際拉壓強度試驗。以保留試體的實測強度驗證成熟度推估。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Integrate concrete temperature histories rather than ambient averages and calibrate with same-mixture specimens of different ages. Check moisture curing and high-temperature exposure against the calibration range and retain direct tensile and compressive tests. Validate maturity-based estimates against directly measured strength of retained specimens. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以成熟度與強度校正編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。用現場溫度歷線積分而非平均氣溫，與同配比不同齡期試體建立關係；另核對濕養護和高溫歷程是否超出校正範圍，保留實際拉壓強度試驗。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for maturity and strength calibration, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Integrate concrete temperature histories rather than ambient averages and calibrate with same-mixture specimens of different ages. Check moisture curing and high-temperature exposure against the calibration range and retain direct tensile and compressive tests.","failure":"注意干擾：高早期溫度可能改變後期強度發展，乾燥也可能中斷水化。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: High early temperature can alter later strength development, and drying can interrupt hydration. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用現場溫度歷線積分而非平均氣溫，與同配比不同齡期試體建立關係；另核對濕養護和高溫歷程是否超出校正範圍，保留實際拉壓強度試驗。以保留試體的實測強度驗證成熟度推估。","textEn":"Integrate concrete temperature histories rather than ambient averages and calibrate with same-mixture specimens of different ages. Check moisture curing and high-temperature exposure against the calibration range and retain direct tensile and compressive tests. Validate maturity-based estimates against directly measured strength of retained specimens.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以成熟度與強度校正編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。用現場溫度歷線積分而非平均氣溫，與同配比不同齡期試體建立關係；另核對濕養護和高溫歷程是否超出校正範圍，保留實際拉壓強度試驗。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for maturity and strength calibration, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Integrate concrete temperature histories rather than ambient averages and calibrate with same-mixture specimens of different ages. Check moisture curing and high-temperature exposure against the calibration range and retain direct tensile and compressive tests.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「成熟度與強度校正」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Maturity and strength calibration\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","接縫剪力能力可以直接等同完整混凝土的強度。","用現場溫度歷線積分而非平均氣溫，與同配比不同齡期試體建立關係；另核對濕養護和高溫歷程是否超出校正範圍，保留實際拉壓強度試驗。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","A construction-joint shear capacity directly equals intact-concrete strength.","Integrate concrete temperature histories rather than ambient averages and calibrate with same-mixture specimens of different ages."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用現場溫度歷線積分而非平均氣溫，與同配比不同齡期試體建立關係；另核對濕養護和高溫歷程是否超出校正範圍，保留實際拉壓強度試驗。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Integrate concrete temperature histories rather than ambient averages and calibrate with same-mixture specimens of different ages. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b231-v15-24","title":"成熟度與強度校正：失效診斷","titleEn":"Maturity and strength calibration: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「成熟度與強度校正」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Maturity and strength calibration” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"高早期溫度可能改變後期強度發展，乾燥也可能中斷水化。若以其他配方成熟度曲線套用，會產生看似精確但缺乏材料依據的承載判讀。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"High early temperature can alter later strength development, and drying can interrupt hydration. Borrowing another mixture maturity curve creates apparently precise capacity estimates without the required material-specific evidence. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若以其他配方成熟度曲線套用，會產生看似精確但缺乏材料依據的承載判讀。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Borrowing another mixture maturity curve creates apparently precise capacity estimates without the required material-specific evidence.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「成熟度達到固定數字就代表所有混凝土具有同一強度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A fixed maturity value means every concrete mixture has the same strength.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"高早期溫度可能改變後期強度發展，乾燥也可能中斷水化。若以其他配方成熟度曲線套用，會產生看似精確但缺乏材料依據的承載判讀。","textEn":"High early temperature can alter later strength development, and drying can interrupt hydration. Borrowing another mixture maturity curve creates apparently precise capacity estimates without the required material-specific evidence.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「成熟度與強度校正」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Maturity and strength calibration\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["高早期溫度可能改變後期強度發展，乾燥也可能中斷水化。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","接縫平均開度很小就能保證止水一定不會漏水。"],"optionsEn":["High early temperature can alter later strength development, and drying can interrupt hydration.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","A small mean joint opening guarantees that the waterstop cannot leak."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高早期溫度可能改變後期強度發展，乾燥也可能中斷水化。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"High early temperature can alter later strength development, and drying can interrupt hydration. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b231-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「接縫開度與止水變形」與「模板側壓與澆置狀態」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Joint opening and waterstop deformation\" and \"Form pressure and placement state\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b231-v15-25","title":"接縫開度與止水變形：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Joint opening and waterstop deformation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「接縫開度與止水變形」如何影響混凝土重力壩分塊澆築的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Joint opening and waterstop deformation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Block-by-block concrete gravity-dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"澆塊收縮使接縫開度改變，止水需要承受法向張開及剪向錯動。只量接縫寬度無法代表三維變形，也不能以材料伸長率直接代替完整接頭性能。 假設有效收縮長20 m、熱膨脹係數10⁻⁵/K、降溫12 K，自由收縮2.4 mm；忽略拘束與相鄰塊共同變形，非止水容許開度。 止水扭曲或接合不良可能在開度不大時漏水，混凝土蜂窩也會繞過完整止水。若只以接縫平均寬度判斷，會漏掉局部錯動與埋設缺陷。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「接縫開度與止水變形」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Block contraction changes joint opening, while waterstops face both normal opening and shear offset. Width alone misses three-dimensional movement, and material elongation is not complete-joint performance. Assume effective contraction length 20 m, expansion coefficient 10⁻⁵/K and cooling 12 K. Free contraction is 2.4 mm, excluding restraint and neighboring-block movement and not an allowable waterstop opening. Twisted or poorly joined waterstops may leak at small openings, while honeycombing bypasses an intact strip. Average joint width misses local shear offsets and defects in embedded placement. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Joint opening and waterstop deformation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設有效收縮長20 m、熱膨脹係數10⁻⁵/K、降溫12 K，自由收縮2.4 mm；忽略拘束與相鄰塊共同變形，非止水容許開度。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume effective contraction length 20 m, expansion coefficient 10⁻⁵/K and cooling 12 K.","failure":"常見誤解：「接縫平均開度很小就能保證止水一定不會漏水。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A small mean joint opening guarantees that the waterstop cannot leak.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「接縫開度與止水變形」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Joint opening and waterstop deformation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-25-k1","title":"接縫開度與止水變形","titleEn":"Joint opening and waterstop deformation","text":"澆塊收縮使接縫開度改變，止水需要承受法向張開及剪向錯動。只量接縫寬度無法代表三維變形，也不能以材料伸長率直接代替完整接頭性能。","textEn":"Block contraction changes joint opening, while waterstops face both normal opening and shear offset. Width alone misses three-dimensional movement, and material elongation is not complete-joint performance.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：接縫平均開度很小就能保證止水一定不會漏水。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A small mean joint opening guarantees that the waterstop cannot leak. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接縫開度與止水變形」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Joint opening and waterstop deformation\" is correct?","options":["接縫平均開度很小就能保證止水一定不會漏水。","澆塊收縮使接縫開度改變，止水需要承受法向張開及剪向錯動。","混凝土剛澆入就已完全自立，所以模板不承受液態側壓。"],"optionsEn":["A small mean joint opening guarantees that the waterstop cannot leak.","Block contraction changes joint opening, while waterstops face both normal opening and shear offset.","Freshly placed concrete is immediately self-supporting and exerts no fluid-like form pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"澆塊收縮使接縫開度改變，止水需要承受法向張開及剪向錯動。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Block contraction changes joint opening, while waterstops face both normal opening and shear offset. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b231-v15-26","title":"接縫開度與止水變形：定量估算","titleEn":"Joint opening and waterstop deformation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「接縫開度與止水變形」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Joint opening and waterstop deformation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設有效收縮長20 m、熱膨脹係數10⁻⁵/K、降溫12 K，自由收縮2.4 mm；忽略拘束與相鄰塊共同變形，非止水容許開度。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume effective contraction length 20 m, expansion coefficient 10⁻⁵/K and cooling 12 K. Free contraction is 2.4 mm, excluding restraint and neighboring-block movement and not an allowable waterstop opening. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：使用多方向接縫計核對張開與剪移，對照兩側溫度和庫水壓；檢查止水埋設位置與接頭試驗是否相符，並用分區漏流辨認局部通道。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use multi-axis joint meters to separate opening and shear, comparing temperatures and reservoir pressure.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設有效收縮長20 m、熱膨脹係數10⁻⁵/K、降溫12 K，自由收縮2.4 mm；忽略拘束與相鄰塊共同變形，非止水容許開度。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume effective contraction length 20 m, expansion coefficient 10⁻⁵/K and cooling 12 K. Free contraction is 2.4 mm, excluding restraint and neighboring-block movement and not an allowable waterstop opening.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「接縫開度與止水變形」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Joint opening and waterstop deformation\", which statement holds?","options":["進料總方量與設計相符就能證明澆塊內完全沒有缺陷。","只要最後總澆置方量正確，局部冷縫就不會影響壩體。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設有效收縮長20 m、熱膨脹係數10⁻⁵/K、降溫12 K，自由收縮2.4 mm；忽略拘束與相鄰塊共同變形，非止水容許開度。"],"optionsEn":["Matching delivered and design volume proves the entire block is defect-free.","Correct final placed volume means local cold joints cannot affect the dam.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume effective contraction length 20 m, expansion coefficient 10⁻⁵/K and cooling 12 K."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設有效收縮長20 m、熱膨脹係數10⁻⁵/K、降溫12 K，自由收縮2.4 mm；忽略拘束與相鄰塊共同變形，非止水容許開度。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume effective contraction length 20 m, expansion coefficient 10⁻⁵/K and cooling 12 K. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b231-v15-27","title":"接縫開度與止水變形：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Joint opening and waterstop deformation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「接縫開度與止水變形」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Joint opening and waterstop deformation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"使用多方向接縫計核對張開與剪移，對照兩側溫度和庫水壓；檢查止水埋設位置與接頭試驗是否相符，並用分區漏流辨認局部通道。把接縫剪移與張開對止水的影響分列。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use multi-axis joint meters to separate opening and shear, comparing temperatures and reservoir pressure. Check waterstop placement against tested joint geometry and use sectional leakage observations to locate preferential paths. Separate the effects of joint shear and opening on waterstop behavior. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以接縫開度與止水變形編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。使用多方向接縫計核對張開與剪移，對照兩側溫度和庫水壓；檢查止水埋設位置與接頭試驗是否相符，並用分區漏流辨認局部通道。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for joint opening and waterstop deformation, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Use multi-axis joint meters to separate opening and shear, comparing temperatures and reservoir pressure. Check waterstop placement against tested joint geometry and use sectional leakage observations to locate preferential paths.","failure":"注意干擾：止水扭曲或接合不良可能在開度不大時漏水，混凝土蜂窩也會繞過完整止水。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Twisted or poorly joined waterstops may leak at small openings, while honeycombing bypasses an intact strip. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"使用多方向接縫計核對張開與剪移，對照兩側溫度和庫水壓；檢查止水埋設位置與接頭試驗是否相符，並用分區漏流辨認局部通道。把接縫剪移與張開對止水的影響分列。","textEn":"Use multi-axis joint meters to separate opening and shear, comparing temperatures and reservoir pressure. Check waterstop placement against tested joint geometry and use sectional leakage observations to locate preferential paths. Separate the effects of joint shear and opening on waterstop behavior.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以接縫開度與止水變形編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。使用多方向接縫計核對張開與剪移，對照兩側溫度和庫水壓；檢查止水埋設位置與接頭試驗是否相符，並用分區漏流辨認局部通道。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for joint opening and waterstop deformation, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Use multi-axis joint meters to separate opening and shear, comparing temperatures and reservoir pressure. Check waterstop placement against tested joint geometry and use sectional leakage observations to locate preferential paths.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「接縫開度與止水變形」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Joint opening and waterstop deformation\"?","options":["使用多方向接縫計核對張開與剪移，對照兩側溫度和庫水壓；檢查止水埋設位置與接頭試驗是否相符，並用分區漏流辨認局部通道。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","澆塊厚度加倍只會讓熱擴散時間加倍。"],"optionsEn":["Use multi-axis joint meters to separate opening and shear, comparing temperatures and reservoir pressure.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Doubling block thickness only doubles the thermal diffusion time."],"answer":0,"explanation":"使用多方向接縫計核對張開與剪移，對照兩側溫度和庫水壓；檢查止水埋設位置與接頭試驗是否相符，並用分區漏流辨認局部通道。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use multi-axis joint meters to separate opening and shear, comparing temperatures and reservoir pressure. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b231-v15-28","title":"接縫開度與止水變形：失效診斷","titleEn":"Joint opening and waterstop deformation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「接縫開度與止水變形」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Joint opening and waterstop deformation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"止水扭曲或接合不良可能在開度不大時漏水，混凝土蜂窩也會繞過完整止水。若只以接縫平均寬度判斷，會漏掉局部錯動與埋設缺陷。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Twisted or poorly joined waterstops may leak at small openings, while honeycombing bypasses an intact strip. Average joint width misses local shear offsets and defects in embedded placement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若只以接縫平均寬度判斷，會漏掉局部錯動與埋設缺陷。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Average joint width misses local shear offsets and defects in embedded placement.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「接縫平均開度很小就能保證止水一定不會漏水。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A small mean joint opening guarantees that the waterstop cannot leak.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"止水扭曲或接合不良可能在開度不大時漏水，混凝土蜂窩也會繞過完整止水。若只以接縫平均寬度判斷，會漏掉局部錯動與埋設缺陷。","textEn":"Twisted or poorly joined waterstops may leak at small openings, while honeycombing bypasses an intact strip. Average joint width misses local shear offsets and defects in embedded placement.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接縫開度與止水變形」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Joint opening and waterstop deformation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","止水扭曲或接合不良可能在開度不大時漏水，混凝土蜂窩也會繞過完整止水。","混凝土剛澆入就已完全自立，所以模板不承受液態側壓。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Twisted or poorly joined waterstops may leak at small openings, while honeycombing bypasses an intact strip.","Freshly placed concrete is immediately self-supporting and exerts no fluid-like form pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"止水扭曲或接合不良可能在開度不大時漏水，混凝土蜂窩也會繞過完整止水。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Twisted or poorly joined waterstops may leak at small openings, while honeycombing bypasses an intact strip. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b231-v15-29","title":"模板側壓與澆置狀態：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Form pressure and placement state: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「模板側壓與澆置狀態」如何影響混凝土重力壩分塊澆築的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Form pressure and placement state” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Block-by-block concrete gravity-dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"新拌混凝土對模板的側壓取決於澆置速率、凝結與振動，短時間內可近似液體。把已硬化混凝土的側向性質拿來估新拌壓力會嚴重失真。 假設新拌混凝土容重24 kN/m³、液態有效高3 m，底壓72 kPa；每米寬合力γh²/2=108 kN/m，作靜水上界示例。 延緩凝結或重新振動可能延長液態壓力作用，局部供料堆高也會增加側壓。只按平均澆築高估算而忽略局部集中，會低估模板與拉桿需求。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「模板側壓與澆置狀態」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Fresh-concrete form pressure depends on placing rate, setting and vibration and may initially approximate a liquid. Hardened-concrete lateral behavior cannot represent the fresh material pressure field. Assume fresh-concrete unit weight 24 kN/m³ and effective fluid height 3 m. Base pressure is 72 kPa and resultant per width is 108 kN/m, as a hydrostatic-bound example. Retarded setting or revibration can prolong fluid-like pressure, while local placement piles increase head. Average lift height can miss local concentrations and understate demand on formwork and ties. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Form pressure and placement state” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設新拌混凝土容重24 kN/m³、液態有效高3 m，底壓72 kPa；每米寬合力γh²/2=108 kN/m，作靜水上界示例。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume fresh-concrete unit weight 24 kN/m³ and effective fluid height 3 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「混凝土剛澆入就已完全自立，所以模板不承受液態側壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Freshly placed concrete is immediately self-supporting and exerts no fluid-like form pressure.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「模板側壓與澆置狀態」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Form pressure and placement state”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-29-k1","title":"模板側壓與澆置狀態","titleEn":"Form pressure and placement state","text":"新拌混凝土對模板的側壓取決於澆置速率、凝結與振動，短時間內可近似液體。把已硬化混凝土的側向性質拿來估新拌壓力會嚴重失真。","textEn":"Fresh-concrete form pressure depends on placing rate, setting and vibration and may initially approximate a liquid. Hardened-concrete lateral behavior cannot represent the fresh material pressure field.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：混凝土剛澆入就已完全自立，所以模板不承受液態側壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Freshly placed concrete is immediately self-supporting and exerts no fluid-like form pressure. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「模板側壓與澆置狀態」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Form pressure and placement state\" is correct?","options":["混凝土剛澆入就已完全自立，所以模板不承受液態側壓。","圖面有排水孔就能不量孔壓而忽略全部基底上浮。","新拌混凝土對模板的側壓取決於澆置速率、凝結與振動，短時間內可近似液體。"],"optionsEn":["Freshly placed concrete is immediately self-supporting and exerts no fluid-like form pressure.","Drains shown on drawings allow all foundation uplift to be ignored without pressure measurements.","Fresh-concrete form pressure depends on placing rate, setting and vibration and may initially approximate a liquid."],"answer":2,"explanation":"新拌混凝土對模板的側壓取決於澆置速率、凝結與振動，短時間內可近似液體。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Fresh-concrete form pressure depends on placing rate, setting and vibration and may initially approximate a liquid. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b231-v15-30","title":"模板側壓與澆置狀態：定量估算","titleEn":"Form pressure and placement state: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「模板側壓與澆置狀態」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Form pressure and placement state” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設新拌混凝土容重24 kN/m³、液態有效高3 m，底壓72 kPa；每米寬合力γh²/2=108 kN/m，作靜水上界示例。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume fresh-concrete unit weight 24 kN/m³ and effective fluid height 3 m. Base pressure is 72 kPa and resultant per width is 108 kN/m, as a hydrostatic-bound example. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對澆置速率、料溫與凝結試驗，將模板壓力計讀數按高度作圖；檢查振動期間峰值與拉桿反力，並確認壓力假設涵蓋實際材料工作性。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check placing rate, temperature and setting tests and plot measured form pressures by elevation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設新拌混凝土容重24 kN/m³、液態有效高3 m，底壓72 kPa；每米寬合力γh²/2=108 kN/m，作靜水上界示例。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume fresh-concrete unit weight 24 kN/m³ and effective fluid height 3 m. Base pressure is 72 kPa and resultant per width is 108 kN/m, as a hydrostatic-bound example.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「模板側壓與澆置狀態」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Form pressure and placement state\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設新拌混凝土容重24 kN/m³、液態有效高3 m，底壓72 kPa。","絕熱溫升就是工地澆塊必定量到的最高溫度。","接縫剪力能力可以直接等同完整混凝土的強度。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume fresh-concrete unit weight 24 kN/m³ and effective fluid height 3 m.","Adiabatic temperature rise is the highest temperature that every placed block must reach.","A construction-joint shear capacity directly equals intact-concrete strength."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設新拌混凝土容重24 kN/m³、液態有效高3 m，底壓72 kPa；每米寬合力γh²/2=108 kN/m，作靜水上界示例。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume fresh-concrete unit weight 24 kN/m³ and effective fluid height 3 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b231-v15-31","title":"模板側壓與澆置狀態：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Form pressure and placement state: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「模板側壓與澆置狀態」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Form pressure and placement state” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對澆置速率、料溫與凝結試驗，將模板壓力計讀數按高度作圖；檢查振動期間峰值與拉桿反力，並確認壓力假設涵蓋實際材料工作性。檢查模板拉桿反力總和是否符合側壓積分。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check placing rate, temperature and setting tests and plot measured form pressures by elevation. Examine vibration-related peaks and tie reactions, confirming that pressure assumptions cover the actual mixture workability. Check whether summed form-tie reactions match the integrated lateral pressure. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以模板側壓與澆置狀態編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。核對澆置速率、料溫與凝結試驗，將模板壓力計讀數按高度作圖；檢查振動期間峰值與拉桿反力，並確認壓力假設涵蓋實際材料工作性。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for form pressure and placement state, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Check placing rate, temperature and setting tests and plot measured form pressures by elevation. Examine vibration-related peaks and tie reactions, confirming that pressure assumptions cover the actual mixture workability.","failure":"注意干擾：延緩凝結或重新振動可能延長液態壓力作用，局部供料堆高也會增加側壓。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Retarded setting or revibration can prolong fluid-like pressure, while local placement piles increase head. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對澆置速率、料溫與凝結試驗，將模板壓力計讀數按高度作圖；檢查振動期間峰值與拉桿反力，並確認壓力假設涵蓋實際材料工作性。檢查模板拉桿反力總和是否符合側壓積分。","textEn":"Check placing rate, temperature and setting tests and plot measured form pressures by elevation. Examine vibration-related peaks and tie reactions, confirming that pressure assumptions cover the actual mixture workability. Check whether summed form-tie reactions match the integrated lateral pressure.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以模板側壓與澆置狀態編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。核對澆置速率、料溫與凝結試驗，將模板壓力計讀數按高度作圖；檢查振動期間峰值與拉桿反力，並確認壓力假設涵蓋實際材料工作性。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for form pressure and placement state, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Check placing rate, temperature and setting tests and plot measured form pressures by elevation. Examine vibration-related peaks and tie reactions, confirming that pressure assumptions cover the actual mixture workability.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「模板側壓與澆置狀態」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Form pressure and placement state\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","核對澆置速率、料溫與凝結試驗，將模板壓力計讀數按高度作圖；檢查振動期間峰值與拉桿反力，並確認壓力假設涵蓋實際材料工作性。","只要冷卻水流量夠大，便能保證混凝土沒有溫差裂縫。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Check placing rate, temperature and setting tests and plot measured form pressures by elevation.","Sufficiently high cooling-water flow guarantees freedom from thermal-gradient cracking."],"answer":1,"explanation":"核對澆置速率、料溫與凝結試驗，將模板壓力計讀數按高度作圖；檢查振動期間峰值與拉桿反力，並確認壓力假設涵蓋實際材料工作性。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check placing rate, temperature and setting tests and plot measured form pressures by elevation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b231-v15-32","title":"模板側壓與澆置狀態：失效診斷","titleEn":"Form pressure and placement state: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「模板側壓與澆置狀態」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Form pressure and placement state” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"延緩凝結或重新振動可能延長液態壓力作用，局部供料堆高也會增加側壓。只按平均澆築高估算而忽略局部集中，會低估模板與拉桿需求。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Retarded setting or revibration can prolong fluid-like pressure, while local placement piles increase head. Average lift height can miss local concentrations and understate demand on formwork and ties. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只按平均澆築高估算而忽略局部集中，會低估模板與拉桿需求。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Average lift height can miss local concentrations and understate demand on formwork and ties.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「混凝土剛澆入就已完全自立，所以模板不承受液態側壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Freshly placed concrete is immediately self-supporting and exerts no fluid-like form pressure.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"延緩凝結或重新振動可能延長液態壓力作用，局部供料堆高也會增加側壓。只按平均澆築高估算而忽略局部集中，會低估模板與拉桿需求。","textEn":"Retarded setting or revibration can prolong fluid-like pressure, while local placement piles increase head. Average lift height can miss local concentrations and understate demand on formwork and ties.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「模板側壓與澆置狀態」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Form pressure and placement state\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","圖面有排水孔就能不量孔壓而忽略全部基底上浮。","延緩凝結或重新振動可能延長液態壓力作用，局部供料堆高也會增加側壓。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Drains shown on drawings allow all foundation uplift to be ignored without pressure measurements.","Retarded setting or revibration can prolong fluid-like pressure, while local placement piles increase head."],"answer":2,"explanation":"延緩凝結或重新振動可能延長液態壓力作用，局部供料堆高也會增加側壓。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Retarded setting or revibration can prolong fluid-like pressure, while local placement piles increase head. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b231-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「上浮折減與抗滑」與「澆塊幾何與材料追溯」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Uplift reduction and sliding\" and \"Block geometry and material traceability\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b231-v15-33","title":"上浮折減與抗滑：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Uplift reduction and sliding: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「上浮折減與抗滑」如何影響混凝土重力壩分塊澆築的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Uplift reduction and sliding” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Block-by-block concrete gravity-dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"重力壩的自重提供摩擦抗滑，但基底上浮降低有效正向力。排水效果需由孔壓驗證，不能因設計有排水孔就自動採取最大折減。 假設每米壩段重量12 MN/m、上浮3 MN/m、μ=0.7、水平推力4 MN/m，純摩擦比μ(W−U)/H=1.575；未含黏聚與地震。 排水量變小可能代表堵塞而非更防水，孔壓升高會讓摩擦比降低。若把排水孔附近低壓當整個基底均值，會過度樂觀估計有效重量與抗滑能力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「上浮折減與抗滑」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Gravity-dam weight provides frictional resistance, but uplift reduces effective normal force. Drainage effectiveness requires pressure evidence rather than an automatic maximum reduction because drains appear on drawings. Assume per-metre weight 12 MN/m, uplift 3 MN/m, μ=0.7 and horizontal force 4 MN/m. Friction-only ratio μ(W−U)/H=1.575, excluding cohesion and earthquake loading. Lower drainage may indicate clogging rather than improved impermeability, and rising pressure lowers frictional reserve. Extrapolating low pressure beside drains across the whole base overstates effective weight and sliding resistance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Uplift reduction and sliding” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設每米壩段重量12 MN/m、上浮3 MN/m、μ=0.7、水平推力4 MN/m，純摩擦比μ(W−U)/H=1.575；未含黏聚與地震。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume per-metre weight 12 MN/m, uplift 3 MN/m, μ=0.7 and horizontal force 4 MN/m.","failure":"常見誤解：「圖面有排水孔就能不量孔壓而忽略全部基底上浮。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Drains shown on drawings allow all foundation uplift to be ignored without pressure measurements.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「上浮折減與抗滑」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Uplift reduction and sliding”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-33-k1","title":"上浮折減與抗滑","titleEn":"Uplift reduction and sliding","text":"重力壩的自重提供摩擦抗滑，但基底上浮降低有效正向力。排水效果需由孔壓驗證，不能因設計有排水孔就自動採取最大折減。","textEn":"Gravity-dam weight provides frictional resistance, but uplift reduces effective normal force. Drainage effectiveness requires pressure evidence rather than an automatic maximum reduction because drains appear on drawings.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：圖面有排水孔就能不量孔壓而忽略全部基底上浮。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Drains shown on drawings allow all foundation uplift to be ignored without pressure measurements. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「上浮折減與抗滑」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Uplift reduction and sliding\" is correct?","options":["重力壩的自重提供摩擦抗滑，但基底上浮降低有效正向力。","圖面有排水孔就能不量孔壓而忽略全部基底上浮。","進料總方量與設計相符就能證明澆塊內完全沒有缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["Gravity-dam weight provides frictional resistance, but uplift reduces effective normal force.","Drains shown on drawings allow all foundation uplift to be ignored without pressure measurements.","Matching delivered and design volume proves the entire block is defect-free."],"answer":0,"explanation":"重力壩的自重提供摩擦抗滑，但基底上浮降低有效正向力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Gravity-dam weight provides frictional resistance, but uplift reduces effective normal force. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b231-v15-34","title":"上浮折減與抗滑：定量估算","titleEn":"Uplift reduction and sliding: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「上浮折減與抗滑」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Uplift reduction and sliding” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設每米壩段重量12 MN/m、上浮3 MN/m、μ=0.7、水平推力4 MN/m，純摩擦比μ(W−U)/H=1.575；未含黏聚與地震。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume per-metre weight 12 MN/m, uplift 3 MN/m, μ=0.7 and horizontal force 4 MN/m. Friction-only ratio μ(W−U)/H=1.575, excluding cohesion and earthquake loading. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：沿基底量測孔壓並積分上浮，對照排水量和庫位變化；確認滑動面位置、材料參數與荷載組合一致，再比較排水減弱時的敏感度，而非只驗一個數字。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Integrate measured basal pressure into uplift and compare drainage and reservoir changes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設每米壩段重量12 MN/m、上浮3 MN/m、μ=0.7、水平推力4 MN/m，純摩擦比μ(W−U)/H=1.575；未含黏聚與地震。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume per-metre weight 12 MN/m, uplift 3 MN/m, μ=0.7 and horizontal force 4 MN/m. Friction-only ratio μ(W−U)/H=1.575, excluding cohesion and earthquake loading.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「上浮折減與抗滑」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Uplift reduction and sliding\", which statement holds?","options":["只要最後總澆置方量正確，局部冷縫就不會影響壩體。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設每米壩段重量12 MN/m、上浮3 MN/m、μ=0.7、水平推力4 MN/m，純摩擦比μ(W−U)/H=1.575。","澆塊厚度加倍只會讓熱擴散時間加倍。"],"optionsEn":["Correct final placed volume means local cold joints cannot affect the dam.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume per-metre weight 12 MN/m, uplift 3 MN/m, μ=0.7 and horizontal force 4 MN/m.","Doubling block thickness only doubles the thermal diffusion time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設每米壩段重量12 MN/m、上浮3 MN/m、μ=0.7、水平推力4 MN/m，純摩擦比μ(W−U)/H=1.575；未含黏聚與地震。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume per-metre weight 12 MN/m, uplift 3 MN/m, μ=0.7 and horizontal force 4 MN/m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b231-v15-35","title":"上浮折減與抗滑：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Uplift reduction and sliding: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「上浮折減與抗滑」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Uplift reduction and sliding” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"沿基底量測孔壓並積分上浮，對照排水量和庫位變化；確認滑動面位置、材料參數與荷載組合一致，再比較排水減弱時的敏感度，而非只驗一個數字。將堵塞情境下上浮分布另做整體力矩檢查。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Integrate measured basal pressure into uplift and compare drainage and reservoir changes. Keep slip plane, material parameters and load combination consistent, then assess sensitivity to impaired drainage instead of checking one ratio alone. Check global moments separately using an uplift distribution representing blocked drains. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以上浮折減與抗滑編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。沿基底量測孔壓並積分上浮，對照排水量和庫位變化；確認滑動面位置、材料參數與荷載組合一致，再比較排水減弱時的敏感度，而非只驗一個數字。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for uplift reduction and sliding, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Integrate measured basal pressure into uplift and compare drainage and reservoir changes. Keep slip plane, material parameters and load combination consistent, then assess sensitivity to impaired drainage instead of checking one ratio alone.","failure":"注意干擾：排水量變小可能代表堵塞而非更防水，孔壓升高會讓摩擦比降低。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Lower drainage may indicate clogging rather than improved impermeability, and rising pressure lowers frictional reserve. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"沿基底量測孔壓並積分上浮，對照排水量和庫位變化；確認滑動面位置、材料參數與荷載組合一致，再比較排水減弱時的敏感度，而非只驗一個數字。將堵塞情境下上浮分布另做整體力矩檢查。","textEn":"Integrate measured basal pressure into uplift and compare drainage and reservoir changes. Keep slip plane, material parameters and load combination consistent, then assess sensitivity to impaired drainage instead of checking one ratio alone. Check global moments separately using an uplift distribution representing blocked drains.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以上浮折減與抗滑編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。沿基底量測孔壓並積分上浮，對照排水量和庫位變化；確認滑動面位置、材料參數與荷載組合一致，再比較排水減弱時的敏感度，而非只驗一個數字。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for uplift reduction and sliding, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Integrate measured basal pressure into uplift and compare drainage and reservoir changes. Keep slip plane, material parameters and load combination consistent, then assess sensitivity to impaired drainage instead of checking one ratio alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「上浮折減與抗滑」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Uplift reduction and sliding\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","成熟度達到固定數字就代表所有混凝土具有同一強度。","沿基底量測孔壓並積分上浮，對照排水量和庫位變化；確認滑動面位置、材料參數與荷載組合一致，再比較排水減弱時的敏感度，而非只驗一個數字。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A fixed maturity value means every concrete mixture has the same strength.","Integrate measured basal pressure into uplift and compare drainage and reservoir changes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"沿基底量測孔壓並積分上浮，對照排水量和庫位變化；確認滑動面位置、材料參數與荷載組合一致，再比較排水減弱時的敏感度，而非只驗一個數字。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Integrate measured basal pressure into uplift and compare drainage and reservoir changes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b231-v15-36","title":"上浮折減與抗滑：失效診斷","titleEn":"Uplift reduction and sliding: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「上浮折減與抗滑」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Uplift reduction and sliding” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"排水量變小可能代表堵塞而非更防水，孔壓升高會讓摩擦比降低。若把排水孔附近低壓當整個基底均值，會過度樂觀估計有效重量與抗滑能力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Lower drainage may indicate clogging rather than improved impermeability, and rising pressure lowers frictional reserve. Extrapolating low pressure beside drains across the whole base overstates effective weight and sliding resistance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若把排水孔附近低壓當整個基底均值，會過度樂觀估計有效重量與抗滑能力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Extrapolating low pressure beside drains across the whole base overstates effective weight and sliding resistance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「圖面有排水孔就能不量孔壓而忽略全部基底上浮。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Drains shown on drawings allow all foundation uplift to be ignored without pressure measurements.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"排水量變小可能代表堵塞而非更防水，孔壓升高會讓摩擦比降低。若把排水孔附近低壓當整個基底均值，會過度樂觀估計有效重量與抗滑能力。","textEn":"Lower drainage may indicate clogging rather than improved impermeability, and rising pressure lowers frictional reserve. Extrapolating low pressure beside drains across the whole base overstates effective weight and sliding resistance.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「上浮折減與抗滑」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Uplift reduction and sliding\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["排水量變小可能代表堵塞而非更防水，孔壓升高會讓摩擦比降低。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","進料總方量與設計相符就能證明澆塊內完全沒有缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["Lower drainage may indicate clogging rather than improved impermeability, and rising pressure lowers frictional reserve.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Matching delivered and design volume proves the entire block is defect-free."],"answer":0,"explanation":"排水量變小可能代表堵塞而非更防水，孔壓升高會讓摩擦比降低。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Lower drainage may indicate clogging rather than improved impermeability, and rising pressure lowers frictional reserve. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b231-v15-37","title":"澆塊幾何與材料追溯：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Block geometry and material traceability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「澆塊幾何與材料追溯」如何影響混凝土重力壩分塊澆築的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Block geometry and material traceability” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Block-by-block concrete gravity-dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"分塊施工讓每一批混凝土對應空間位置，幾何方量與材料紀錄可互相驗證。超澆、孔洞和預留廊道會影響方量，不能用進料量直接當完成實體。 假設矩形澆塊20×15×2 m，扣除廊道30 m³，淨量570 m³；若供料590 m³，差20 m³須查損耗和幾何，不能直接稱空洞。 把運輸損耗或模板外擴誤判為內部空洞會導致錯誤調查，反過來總量吻合也可能掩蓋局部蜂窩。空間追溯能找出缺陷位置，總方量卻無法。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「澆塊幾何與材料追溯」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Block construction links concrete batches to spatial locations, enabling geometric and material records to cross-check. Overpour, voids and galleries affect volume, so delivered material is not automatically completed solid geometry. Assume block 20×15×2 m minus gallery 30 m³, giving net 570 m³. Delivery 590 m³ leaves a 20 m³ difference requiring geometry and loss checks, not an automatic void diagnosis. Transport loss or form bulging can be mistaken for voids, while matching total volume can conceal local honeycombing. Spatial traceability can locate defects, whereas aggregate quantity cannot resolve their distribution. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Block geometry and material traceability” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設矩形澆塊20×15×2 m，扣除廊道30 m³，淨量570 m³；若供料590 m³，差20 m³須查損耗和幾何，不能直接稱空洞。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume block 20×15×2 m minus gallery 30 m³, giving net 570 m³.","failure":"常見誤解：「進料總方量與設計相符就能證明澆塊內完全沒有缺陷。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Matching delivered and design volume proves the entire block is defect-free.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「澆塊幾何與材料追溯」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Block geometry and material traceability”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-37-k1","title":"澆塊幾何與材料追溯","titleEn":"Block geometry and material traceability","text":"分塊施工讓每一批混凝土對應空間位置，幾何方量與材料紀錄可互相驗證。超澆、孔洞和預留廊道會影響方量，不能用進料量直接當完成實體。","textEn":"Block construction links concrete batches to spatial locations, enabling geometric and material records to cross-check. Overpour, voids and galleries affect volume, so delivered material is not automatically completed solid geometry.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：進料總方量與設計相符就能證明澆塊內完全沒有缺陷。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Matching delivered and design volume proves the entire block is defect-free. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「澆塊幾何與材料追溯」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Block geometry and material traceability\" is correct?","options":["進料總方量與設計相符就能證明澆塊內完全沒有缺陷。","分塊施工讓每一批混凝土對應空間位置，幾何方量與材料紀錄可互相驗證。","絕熱溫升就是工地澆塊必定量到的最高溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Matching delivered and design volume proves the entire block is defect-free.","Block construction links concrete batches to spatial locations, enabling geometric and material records to cross-check.","Adiabatic temperature rise is the highest temperature that every placed block must reach."],"answer":1,"explanation":"分塊施工讓每一批混凝土對應空間位置，幾何方量與材料紀錄可互相驗證。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Block construction links concrete batches to spatial locations, enabling geometric and material records to cross-check. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b231-v15-38","title":"澆塊幾何與材料追溯：定量估算","titleEn":"Block geometry and material traceability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「澆塊幾何與材料追溯」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Block geometry and material traceability” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設矩形澆塊20×15×2 m，扣除廊道30 m³，淨量570 m³；若供料590 m³，差20 m³須查損耗和幾何，不能直接稱空洞。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume block 20×15×2 m minus gallery 30 m³, giving net 570 m³. Delivery 590 m³ leaves a 20 m³ difference requiring geometry and loss checks, not an automatic void diagnosis. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把測量面、預留件和批次進料分別建帳，核對每車時間與澆築位置；以收方幾何、廢料紀錄和密度試驗做閉合，對不能解釋的差異要求獨立查證。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Maintain separate surveyed surfaces, embedded-volume and delivery records, matching batches to placement location.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設矩形澆塊20×15×2 m，扣除廊道30 m³，淨量570 m³；若供料590 m³，差20 m³須查損耗和幾何，不能直接稱空洞。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume block 20×15×2 m minus gallery 30 m³, giving net 570 m³. Delivery 590 m³ leaves a 20 m³ difference requiring geometry and loss checks, not an automatic void diagnosis.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「澆塊幾何與材料追溯」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Block geometry and material traceability\", which statement holds?","options":["接縫剪力能力可以直接等同完整混凝土的強度。","只要冷卻水流量夠大，便能保證混凝土沒有溫差裂縫。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設矩形澆塊20×15×2 m，扣除廊道30 m³，淨量570 m³。"],"optionsEn":["A construction-joint shear capacity directly equals intact-concrete strength.","Sufficiently high cooling-water flow guarantees freedom from thermal-gradient cracking.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume block 20×15×2 m minus gallery 30 m³, giving net 570 m³."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設矩形澆塊20×15×2 m，扣除廊道30 m³，淨量570 m³；若供料590 m³，差20 m³須查損耗和幾何，不能直接稱空洞。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume block 20×15×2 m minus gallery 30 m³, giving net 570 m³. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b231-v15-39","title":"澆塊幾何與材料追溯：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Block geometry and material traceability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「澆塊幾何與材料追溯」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Block geometry and material traceability” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把測量面、預留件和批次進料分別建帳，核對每車時間與澆築位置；以收方幾何、廢料紀錄和密度試驗做閉合，對不能解釋的差異要求獨立查證。對差異最大的批次回查供料和廢料原始憑據。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Maintain separate surveyed surfaces, embedded-volume and delivery records, matching batches to placement location. Close quantities using as-built geometry, waste records and density tests, requiring independent evidence for unexplained differences. Revisit original delivery and waste records for batches with the largest discrepancies. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以澆塊幾何與材料追溯編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。把測量面、預留件和批次進料分別建帳，核對每車時間與澆築位置；以收方幾何、廢料紀錄和密度試驗做閉合，對不能解釋的差異要求獨立查證。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for block geometry and material traceability, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Maintain separate surveyed surfaces, embedded-volume and delivery records, matching batches to placement location. Close quantities using as-built geometry, waste records and density tests, requiring independent evidence for unexplained differences.","failure":"注意干擾：把運輸損耗或模板外擴誤判為內部空洞會導致錯誤調查，反過來總量吻合也可能掩蓋局部蜂窩。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Transport loss or form bulging can be mistaken for voids, while matching total volume can conceal local honeycombing. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把測量面、預留件和批次進料分別建帳，核對每車時間與澆築位置；以收方幾何、廢料紀錄和密度試驗做閉合，對不能解釋的差異要求獨立查證。對差異最大的批次回查供料和廢料原始憑據。","textEn":"Maintain separate surveyed surfaces, embedded-volume and delivery records, matching batches to placement location. Close quantities using as-built geometry, waste records and density tests, requiring independent evidence for unexplained differences. Revisit original delivery and waste records for batches with the largest discrepancies.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以澆塊幾何與材料追溯編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。把測量面、預留件和批次進料分別建帳，核對每車時間與澆築位置；以收方幾何、廢料紀錄和密度試驗做閉合，對不能解釋的差異要求獨立查證。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for block geometry and material traceability, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Maintain separate surveyed surfaces, embedded-volume and delivery records, matching batches to placement location. Close quantities using as-built geometry, waste records and density tests, requiring independent evidence for unexplained differences.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「澆塊幾何與材料追溯」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Block geometry and material traceability\"?","options":["把測量面、預留件和批次進料分別建帳，核對每車時間與澆築位置；以收方幾何、廢料紀錄和密度試驗做閉合，對不能解釋的差異要求獨立查證。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","接縫平均開度很小就能保證止水一定不會漏水。"],"optionsEn":["Maintain separate surveyed surfaces, embedded-volume and delivery records, matching batches to placement location.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A small mean joint opening guarantees that the waterstop cannot leak."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把測量面、預留件和批次進料分別建帳，核對每車時間與澆築位置；以收方幾何、廢料紀錄和密度試驗做閉合，對不能解釋的差異要求獨立查證。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Maintain separate surveyed surfaces, embedded-volume and delivery records, matching batches to placement location. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b231-v15-40","title":"澆塊幾何與材料追溯：失效診斷","titleEn":"Block geometry and material traceability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b231-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「澆塊幾何與材料追溯」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Block geometry and material traceability” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把運輸損耗或模板外擴誤判為內部空洞會導致錯誤調查，反過來總量吻合也可能掩蓋局部蜂窩。空間追溯能找出缺陷位置，總方量卻無法。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Transport loss or form bulging can be mistaken for voids, while matching total volume can conceal local honeycombing. Spatial traceability can locate defects, whereas aggregate quantity cannot resolve their distribution. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：空間追溯能找出缺陷位置，總方量卻無法。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Spatial traceability can locate defects, whereas aggregate quantity cannot resolve their distribution.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「進料總方量與設計相符就能證明澆塊內完全沒有缺陷。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Matching delivered and design volume proves the entire block is defect-free.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b231-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把運輸損耗或模板外擴誤判為內部空洞會導致錯誤調查，反過來總量吻合也可能掩蓋局部蜂窩。空間追溯能找出缺陷位置，總方量卻無法。","textEn":"Transport loss or form bulging can be mistaken for voids, while matching total volume can conceal local honeycombing. Spatial traceability can locate defects, whereas aggregate quantity cannot resolve their distribution.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]},{"id":"b231-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「澆塊幾何與材料追溯」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Block geometry and material traceability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","把運輸損耗或模板外擴誤判為內部空洞會導致錯誤調查，反過來總量吻合也可能掩蓋局部蜂窩。","絕熱溫升就是工地澆塊必定量到的最高溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Transport loss or form bulging can be mistaken for voids, while matching total volume can conceal local honeycombing.","Adiabatic temperature rise is the highest temperature that every placed block must reach."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把運輸損耗或模板外擴誤判為內部空洞會導致錯誤調查，反過來總量吻合也可能掩蓋局部蜂窩。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Transport loss or form bulging can be mistaken for voids, while matching total volume can conceal local honeycombing. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-rcc"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
